SBS.tree({"name":"","n":95154,"img":"","kids":[{"name":"Fasteners","n":80840,"img":"img/573.png","kids":[{"name":"Screws","n":15496,"img":"img/553.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"553","name":"Machine Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":8582,"img":"img/553.png","desc":"A machine screw is a type of fastener with a uniform thread designed for use in tapping or threading into pre-drilled holes in metal, plastic, or other materials. It is typically used with a nut or directly into a threaded hole to secure parts together in mechanical assemblies.","nf":14},{"id":"557","name":"Self Tapping Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":2024,"img":"img/557.png","desc":"Self-tapping screws are fasteners designed with a sharp, pointed tip that allows them to create their own threads as they are driven into materials, such as wood, plastic, or metal. This eliminates the need for pre-drilled holes, making them ideal for quick and secure fastening in a variety of applications.","nf":16},{"id":"559","name":"Thread Rolling Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":1111,"img":"img/559.png","desc":"Thread rolling screws are a type of fastener that forms threads in the material as they are driven in, rather than cutting or tapping the material. This process creates a stronger, more secure connection by providing a tight fit and reducing the risk of stripping or weakening the material.","nf":19},{"id":"564","name":"Wood Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":982,"img":"img/564.png","desc":"A wood screw is a type of fastener designed with a threaded shaft to be driven into wood, providing a strong, secure hold. It typically features a tapered, pointed tip that allows it to easily penetrate wood without the need for a pilot hole in many cases.","nf":10},{"id":"556","name":"SEMS Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":662,"img":"img/556.png","desc":"A SEMS screw is a pre-assembled fastener that combines a screw and a washer, typically held in place by the screw's threads. This design simplifies assembly, prevents the washer from being lost, and saves time in manufacturing or maintenance processes.","nf":13},{"id":"555","name":"Self Drilling Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":612,"img":"img/555.png","desc":"Self-drilling screws are fasteners designed with a drill-like point that allows them to create their own hole as they are driven into materials, eliminating the need for pre-drilling. They are commonly used in construction and metalworking applications for quick, efficient installation, particularly in sheet metal and other hard materials.","nf":14},{"id":"558","name":"Thread Cutting Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":435,"img":"img/558.png","desc":"Thread cutting screws are fasteners designed with a sharp, cutting edge that allows them to create their own threads when driven into materials such as metal or plastic. They are commonly used in applications where pre-threaded holes are not available or where a secure, self-tapping connection is required.","nf":13},{"id":"560","name":"Thumb Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":336,"img":"img/560.png","desc":"Thumb screws are fasteners with a large, knurled head that allows for manual tightening and loosening without the need for tools. They are commonly used in applications where quick and frequent adjustments are needed, such as in computer equipment or machinery panels.","nf":11},{"id":"552","name":"Lag Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":274,"img":"img/552.png","desc":"Lag screws are heavy-duty, large-threaded fasteners designed for fastening wood to wood or wood to masonry, providing a strong and secure hold. They typically have a hexagonal head and are driven into place with a wrench or power tool, often used in construction and woodworking applications.","nf":10},{"id":"548","name":"Drive Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":128,"img":"img/548.png","desc":"Drive screws are screws designed with a unique, slotted head that allows for easy installation using a drive tool, such as a screwdriver or power drill. They are commonly used in applications requiring quick, secure fastening, often in materials like metal, wood, or plastic.","nf":7},{"id":"562","name":"Weld Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":68,"img":"img/562.png","desc":"Weld screws are fasteners designed to be permanently attached to a workpiece through a welding process, typically used in metal fabrication. They allow for secure fastening without the need for traditional nuts or bolts, providing a strong, vibration-resistant connection in applications like automotive and industrial equipment.","nf":15},{"id":"549","name":"Drywall Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":64,"img":"img/549.png","desc":"Drywall screws are specifically designed fasteners used to attach drywall sheets to wood or metal studs during construction. They feature a sharp point, coarse threads for wood, and fine threads for metal, ensuring a secure hold and minimizing the risk of damage to the drywall.","nf":7},{"id":"988","name":"Tamper Resistant Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":61,"img":"img/988.png","desc":"Tamper-resistant screws are specially designed fasteners that require unique tools or keys to install or remove, preventing unauthorized access or tampering. They are commonly used in security-sensitive applications such as public installations, electronics, and equipment to deter theft or vandalism.","nf":14},{"id":"546","name":"Binding Post","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":44,"img":"img/546.png","desc":"A binding post fastener, also commonly called a \"Chicago screw,\" is a two-part fastening system consisting of a threaded post barrel and a screw that threads into it, used to securely bind materials together by inserting them through holes punched in the material and screwing the two parts together; often used in applications like binding documents, photo albums, or leather goods.","nf":12},{"id":"550","name":"Eye Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":38,"img":"img/550.png","desc":"Eye screws are screws with a looped, ring-shaped head, designed to provide a secure point for attaching ropes, cables, or hooks. They are commonly used in hanging, lifting, and securing applications, providing a versatile anchor for various materials.","nf":7},{"id":"563","name":"Wing Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":26,"img":"img/563.png","desc":"Wing screws are fasteners with two \"wings\" on either side of the head, allowing for easy manual tightening and loosening without the need for tools. They are commonly used in applications where quick adjustments or frequent removal of components are required, such as in machinery, electronics, or household items.","nf":9},{"id":"554","name":"Sealing Screw","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":25,"img":"img/554.png","desc":"A sealing screw is a type of fastener designed with a built-in sealing element, such as an O-ring or gasket, to prevent leaks and protect against moisture, dust, or other contaminants. These screws are often used in applications requiring a secure and airtight or watertight seal, such as in plumbing, automotive, or machinery.","nf":14},{"id":"551","name":"Jack Screws","path":"Fasteners > Screws","n":24,"img":"img/551.png","desc":"Jack screws are fasteners with a threaded shaft and a hexagonal head, designed to adjust the height or position of a component by turning. They are commonly used in mechanical and industrial applications, such as leveling or aligning equipment, and can be operated manually or with a tool.","nf":10}]},{"name":"Sockets","n":15102,"img":"img/573.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"573","name":"Socket Head Cap Screws","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":8718,"img":"img/573.png","desc":"Socket head cap screws are fasteners with a cylindrical head and an internal hexagonal drive, allowing them to be tightened or loosened using an Allen wrench or socket tool. They are commonly used in applications where space is limited or where a clean, flush appearance is required.","nf":16},{"id":"569","name":"Button Socket Cap Screws","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":2142,"img":"img/569.png","desc":"Button socket cap screws are fasteners with a rounded, low-profile head and a hexagonal recess for driving with an Allen wrench. They are commonly used in applications requiring a clean, flush appearance and a secure, high-strength fastening solution.","nf":20},{"id":"571","name":"Flat Socket Cap Screws","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":1964,"img":"img/571.png","desc":"Flat socket cap screws are threaded fasteners with a flat, countersunk head and an internal hex drive, designed to sit flush with or below the surface of the material. They are commonly used in applications requiring a smooth finish and strong, precise fastening.","nf":16},{"id":"570","name":"Captive Screws/Socket Undersized Screws","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":681,"img":"img/570.png","desc":"Captive screws, or socket undersized screws, are fasteners designed to remain attached to a component after installation, preventing loss or misplacement. They typically feature a reduced head size or special design that allows them to stay secured within a socket or housing, often used in electronic and industrial applications.","nf":11},{"id":"572","name":"Low Head Socket Cap Screws","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":644,"img":"img/572.png","desc":"Low head socket cap screws are fasteners with a small, low-profile head and a hexagonal recess, designed for use in tight spaces where a standard cap screw may not fit. They are commonly used in machinery and electronics where space constraints and a clean, flush appearance are required while maintaining strong, secure fastening.","nf":11},{"id":"1312","name":"Truss/Cone Head Socket Cap Screw","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":407,"img":"img/1312.png","desc":"A truss/cone head socket cap screw is a type of fastening screw with a low-profile, rounded head that offers a wide bearing surface for better load distribution. It features an internal hex drive, allowing for a secure, high-torque installation while maintaining a flush or slightly raised profile in assemblies.","nf":16},{"id":"1007","name":"Button Flange Socket Cap Screw","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":274,"img":"img/1007.png","desc":"A button flange socket cap screw is a fastener with a low-profile, rounded button head and an integrated flange that helps distribute the load evenly over a larger surface area. It is typically used in applications where space is tight and a secure, flush fastening is required, such as in machinery, automotive, and electronic assemblies.","nf":11},{"id":"1311","name":"Pan Head Socket Cap Screw","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":245,"img":"img/1311.png","desc":"A pan head socket cap screw is a type of fastener with a rounded, slightly raised head and a hexagonal recess designed for driving with an Allen wrench. It is commonly used in applications that require a strong, secure connection with a larger bearing surface and easy access for tightening","nf":15},{"id":"566","name":"Socket Jam Screws","path":"Fasteners > Sockets","n":27,"img":"img/566.png","desc":"Socket jam screws are screws with a hexagonal socket drive that are used to secure components in place by preventing movement or loosening. They typically feature a pointed tip that digs into the surface, providing a firm grip and ensuring a secure fit.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Bolts","n":13451,"img":"img/187.png","kids":[{"name":"Structural Bolts","n":268,"img":"img/931.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"931","name":"Structural Bolt with Nut","path":"Fasteners > Bolts > Structural Bolts","n":268,"img":"img/931.png","desc":"A structural bolt with a nut is a type of fastening system used in construction to securely join two or more structural components together. The bolt provides the threading to attach the nut, creating a strong, reliable connection that can withstand significant loads and stresses.","nf":10}]}],"cats":[{"id":"187","name":"Hex Cap Screw and Hex Bolt","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":7711,"img":"img/187.png","desc":"A hex cap screw is a type of fastener with a hexagonal head and fully threaded shaft, designed for use with a nut or in a pre-threaded hole to secure parts together. A hex bolt is similar, but it is typically used with a nut and has a partially threaded shaft, making it ideal for applications requiring a secure clamping force.","nf":16},{"id":"192","name":"Flange Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":1580,"img":"img/192.png","desc":"Flange bolts are fasteners with a built-in flange beneath the head, which acts as a washer to distribute the load and prevent the bolt from loosening. They are commonly used in automotive, construction, and machinery applications where a strong, secure, and vibration-resistant connection is needed.","nf":15},{"id":"575","name":"Shoulder Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":1296,"img":"img/575.png","desc":"Shoulder bolts are fasteners with a cylindrical, unthreaded shoulder between the head and the threaded portion, designed to provide precise alignment and support in mechanical assemblies. They are commonly used in applications where rotation or movement is required, such as in pivot points or as a mounting base for other components.","nf":15},{"id":"188","name":"Carriage Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":740,"img":"img/188.png","desc":"Carriage bolts are round-headed fasteners with a square neck beneath the head that prevents rotation when tightened, making them ideal for securing wood to metal or other materials. They are commonly used in construction, outdoor furniture, and automotive applications where a smooth, flush finish is desired.","nf":11},{"id":"203","name":"Tap Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":503,"img":"img/203.png","desc":"Tap bolts are fully threaded bolts with a hexagonal head, designed to be used in pre-tapped holes for secure fastening. They are commonly used in applications where strong, reliable connections are needed, such as in machinery, automotive, and structural assemblies.","nf":14},{"id":"194","name":"Heavy Hex Cap Screws and Heavy Hex Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":364,"img":"img/194.png","desc":"Heavy hex cap screws and heavy hex bolts are high-strength fasteners with a hexagonal head, designed for use in demanding applications requiring increased load-bearing capacity. They are typically used in construction, machinery, and industrial settings, where they provide secure, durable fastening in both threaded and unthreaded holes.","nf":8},{"id":"190","name":"Eye Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":309,"img":"img/190.png","desc":"Eye bolts are fasteners with a circular loop or \"eye\" at one end, designed to provide a secure point for attaching ropes, cables, or other lifting equipment. They are commonly used in lifting, rigging, and anchoring applications where a strong, reliable connection is required for holding or securing loads.","nf":11},{"id":"207","name":"U bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":187,"img":"img/207.png","desc":"U-bolts are U-shaped metal fasteners with threaded ends, designed to secure pipes, rods, or other components to a surface or structure. They are commonly used in automotive, plumbing, and construction applications for mounting or supporting items, providing a strong and stable hold.","nf":9},{"id":"204","name":"Tension Control Bolt","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":139,"img":"img/204.png","desc":"A tension control bolt is a high-strength fastener designed to ensure consistent and precise tension when installed, commonly used in structural steel connections. It features a built-in spline that shears off once the bolt has reached the proper tension, providing a reliable and secure connection without the need for a separate torque measurement.","nf":5},{"id":"200","name":"Square Head Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":109,"img":"img/200.png","desc":"Square head bolts are fasteners with a square-shaped head, designed to provide a larger surface area for tightening with a wrench or other tools. They are commonly used in heavy-duty applications where high torque is needed and are often found in construction, machinery, and outdoor structures.","nf":11},{"id":"193","name":"Hanger Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":55,"img":"img/193.png","desc":"Hanger bolts are fasteners with a wood screw thread on one end and a machine screw thread on the other, designed to attach objects to wood while allowing for secure attachment to other components with nuts or bolts. They are commonly used in construction and plumbing applications for hanging or mounting purposes.","nf":4},{"id":"189","name":"Elevator Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":51,"img":"img/189.png","desc":"Elevator bolts are specialized fasteners with a large, flat, and smooth head designed to provide a secure connection with a wide surface area. They are commonly used in conveyor systems, elevators, and machinery where flat head bolts are needed to prevent snagging and ensure smooth operation.","nf":16},{"id":"191","name":"Ferry Cap Screws","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":39,"img":"img/191.png","desc":"Ferry cap screws are heavy-duty fasteners with a large, rounded head and a fully threaded shaft, designed for use in marine and other high-stress environments. They are typically made from corrosion-resistant materials, ensuring a secure, long-lasting connection in applications exposed to harsh conditions, such as boats or industrial machinery.","nf":10},{"id":"198","name":"Plow Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":39,"img":"img/198.png","desc":"Plow bolts are specialized fasteners with a flat, wide head and a smooth neck designed to prevent the bolt from turning when tightened. They are commonly used in agricultural equipment, such as plows, to secure parts in place while providing a smooth surface that won't catch on materials.","nf":5},{"id":"196","name":"J Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":21,"img":"img/196.png","desc":"J bolts are fasteners shaped like the letter \"J,\" with a hook on one end and a threaded section on the other. They are commonly used in construction and heavy-duty applications to secure objects to a surface, such as anchoring posts, securing machinery, or fastening parts to concrete.","nf":9},{"id":"205","name":"Track Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":14,"img":"img/205.png","desc":"Track bolts are specialized fasteners used to secure rails to railroad ties or other tracks, typically featuring a square or hexagonal head and a long, threaded shaft. They are designed for high strength and durability to withstand the stresses and vibrations associated with rail transportation.","nf":8},{"id":"186","name":"Banjo Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":9,"img":"img/186.png","desc":"Banjo bolts are specialized fasteners with a hollow shaft and one or more holes through the head, designed to allow fluid or gas to pass through. They are commonly used in hydraulic, brake, and fuel systems to connect hoses or pipes to components while maintaining a secure and leak-proof seal.","nf":10},{"id":"927","name":"Heavy Tap Bolt","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":8,"img":"img/927.png","desc":"A heavy tap bolt is a high-strength fastener with a fully threaded shaft and a hexagonal head, designed to be used in applications requiring high load-bearing capacity. It is typically used in structural and heavy machinery applications, where the bolt is inserted into a pre-tapped hole and tightened with a wrench.","nf":5},{"id":"1323","name":"External Torx Flange Screw","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":4,"img":"","desc":"","nf":6},{"id":"206","name":"Truss Head Bolt","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":4,"img":"img/206.png","desc":"A truss head bolt is a type of fastener featuring a low-profile, wide, rounded head designed to distribute the load over a larger surface area. It is commonly used in applications where a large bearing surface is needed, such as in sheet metal or structural assemblies, to prevent damage to the material being fastened.","nf":7},{"id":"199","name":"Sidewalk Bolt","path":"Fasteners > Bolts","n":1,"img":"img/199.png","desc":"A sidewalk bolt is a type of fastener commonly used in outdoor applications, such as securing objects to concrete or pavement. It typically features a large, flat head designed to prevent it from being easily removed and to provide a secure attachment in heavy-duty environments.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Washers","n":7397,"img":"img/1246.png","kids":[{"name":"Flat Washers","n":4760,"img":"img/1246.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1246","name":"Flat Washer","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Flat Washers","n":3915,"img":"img/1246.png","desc":"A flat washer is a thin, disc-shaped fastener used to distribute the load of a screw or bolt evenly across a surface. It helps prevent damage to the material being fastened and ensures a secure, stable connection by reducing friction and preventing the fastener from loosening.","nf":7},{"id":"1024","name":"Shims","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Flat Washers","n":531,"img":"img/1024.png","desc":"Shims are thin, flat pieces of material used to fill gaps or spaces between components to ensure proper alignment, level, or spacing in mechanical assemblies. They are commonly used in construction, automotive, and industrial applications to adjust clearances and improve the precision and stability of equipment.","nf":4},{"id":"1020","name":"Fender Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Flat Washers","n":259,"img":"img/1020.png","desc":"Fender washers are large, flat washers with a wide outer diameter and a smaller inner diameter, designed to distribute the load of a fastener over a larger surface area. They are commonly used to prevent damage to thin or soft materials, such as sheet metal or plastic, when securing bolts or screws.","nf":10},{"id":"1026","name":"Structural Flat Washer","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Flat Washers","n":55,"img":"img/1026.png","desc":"A structural flat washer is a type of washer with a larger outer diameter, designed to distribute the load of a fastener over a wider surface area. It is typically used in heavy-duty applications, such as construction and machinery, to prevent damage to materials and ensure a secure, stable connection.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Lock Washers","n":1479,"img":"img/1031.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1031","name":"Split Lock Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":554,"img":"img/1031.png","desc":"Split lock washers are designed to prevent fasteners from loosening due to vibration or torque by creating tension between the washer and the surface. Their split, coiled design allows the washer to dig into the fastener and the material, providing a secure, friction-based lock.","nf":13},{"id":"1247","name":"External Tooth Lock Washer","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":360,"img":"img/1247.png","desc":"An external tooth lock washer is a type of washer with teeth on the outer edge that dig into the surface of the material being fastened, creating friction to prevent loosening. It is commonly used in applications where vibration or movement could cause fasteners to loosen over time.","nf":14},{"id":"1248","name":"High Collar Lockwasher","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":114,"img":"img/1248.png","desc":"A high collar lockwasher is a type of lockwasher with an elevated, thicker outer edge designed to provide extra resistance against loosening due to vibration or torque. The high collar creates a stronger grip between the washer and the surface, ensuring a more secure and stable fastening in heavy-duty applications.","nf":8},{"id":"1249","name":"Lock Washers Misc..","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":104,"img":"img/1249.png","desc":"Lock washers are specialized washers designed to prevent fasteners from loosening due to vibration or movement. They come in various types, such as internal or external tooth, split, and wave washers, each offering unique methods of gripping and securing fasteners in different applications.","nf":5},{"id":"1032","name":"Spring Lock Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":96,"img":"img/1032.png","desc":"Spring lock washers are a type of locking washer designed to prevent loosening of fasteners due to vibration or movement by providing tension between the bolt and the surface. They are commonly used in mechanical and automotive applications to ensure secure, reliable connections.","nf":5},{"id":"1029","name":"Ribbed Lockwasher","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":66,"img":"img/1029.png","desc":"A ribbed lockwasher is a type of locking washer featuring raised ribs or teeth that dig into the surfaces of the bolt and the material it is fastened to, preventing loosening due to vibration. It is commonly used in mechanical and industrial applications to provide a secure, reliable connection and reduce the risk of fasteners backing out.","nf":8},{"id":"1326","name":"Serration Lock Washer","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":50,"img":"","desc":"","nf":7},{"id":"1035","name":"Wedge Lock Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":46,"img":"img/1035.png","desc":"Wedge lock washers are mechanical fasteners designed to prevent loosening due to vibration or external forces by creating a wedging effect between the washer and the surface. They feature a unique shape with angled teeth that dig into the surfaces, providing a secure and reliable grip.","nf":3},{"id":"1027","name":"Heavy Split Lock Washer","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":45,"img":"img/1027.png","desc":"A heavy split lock washer is a type of mechanical fastener designed to prevent loosening of bolts and nuts by providing tension and friction between the parts. It features a split ring with sharp edges that dig into the surface, ensuring a secure connection in high-vibration or heavy-load applications.","nf":7},{"id":"1270","name":"Curved Split Lock Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers > Lock Washers","n":44,"img":"img/1270.png","desc":"Curved split lock washers are designed to prevent fasteners from loosening due to vibration by providing tension between the washer and the surface. Their split, curved shape creates a spring-like action that locks the fastener in place, making them ideal for use in automotive, machinery, and electrical applications.","nf":2}]}],"cats":[{"id":"581","name":"Belleville Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":426,"img":"img/581.png","desc":"Curved spring washers are a type of lock washer with a curved or wave-like shape, designed to provide tension and prevent loosening of fasteners due to vibration or movement. They are commonly used in mechanical and automotive applications to maintain a secure connection by absorbing shock and maintaining constant pressure.","nf":10},{"id":"595","name":"Wave Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":197,"img":"img/595.png","desc":"Wave washers are mechanical components with a wavy, spring-like design, used to provide load distribution and absorb shock or vibration in various applications. They are commonly used in assemblies to maintain pressure or prevent loosening of parts under dynamic conditions.","nf":6},{"id":"593","name":"Spherical and Conical Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":118,"img":"img/593.png","desc":"Spherical and conical washers are specialized washers designed to provide a stable surface for fasteners, compensating for uneven or irregular surfaces. Spherical washers have a curved shape that allows them to adjust to varying angles, while conical washers have a tapered design that helps to distribute loads evenly and maintain consistent pressure.","nf":7},{"id":"583","name":"Bonded Sealing Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":94,"img":"img/583.png","desc":"Bonded sealing washers are washers that feature a rubber or elastomeric sealing layer bonded to a metal base, designed to create a leak-proof seal when compressed. They are commonly used in applications that require both a secure fastening and resistance to liquids or gases, such as in automotive, plumbing, and hydraulic systems.","nf":10},{"id":"586","name":"Curved Spring Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":65,"img":"img/586.png","desc":"Spherical and conical washers are designed to provide a stable and secure fit between fasteners and uneven or angled surfaces. Spherical washers have a rounded shape to adapt to varying angles, while conical washers have a tapered design that helps evenly distribute loads and maintain pressure in mechanical assemblies.","nf":5},{"id":"1290","name":"Shoulder Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":63,"img":"img/1290.png","desc":"Shoulder washers are specialized washers with a raised, cylindrical shoulder that helps to distribute load and prevent surface damage during fastening. They are commonly used to provide spacing, reduce friction, and isolate parts in mechanical and electrical assemblies.","nf":1},{"id":"582","name":"Beveled Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":62,"img":"img/582.png","desc":"Beveled washers are washers with angled edges, designed to accommodate a surface that is not perfectly flat or is slightly curved. The beveled shape allows for better load distribution and a more secure fit when used in applications where surfaces need to be aligned at an angle.","nf":4},{"id":"588","name":"Finishing Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":53,"img":"img/588.png","desc":"Finishing washers are flat, circular washers used to provide a neat, clean appearance to fastener installations, often covering the rough edges of holes. They are typically used in applications where aesthetic presentation is important, such as in furniture assembly or decorative projects","nf":8},{"id":"592","name":"Retaining Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":23,"img":"img/592.png","desc":"Retaining washers are flat washers designed to prevent the movement or loosening of components, such as bolts or nuts, by holding them in place. They are typically used in applications where vibration or force could cause parts to shift, ensuring a secure and stable assembly.","nf":9},{"id":"594","name":"Tab Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":20,"img":"img/594.png","desc":"Tab washers are flat washers with one or more tabs that can be bent over a fastener to prevent it from loosening. They are commonly used in mechanical and automotive applications to provide extra security by locking bolts, nuts, or other components in place.","nf":5},{"id":"585","name":"Cup Washers","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":14,"img":"img/585.png","desc":"Cup washers are flat washers with a concave, cup-shaped design that helps distribute pressure evenly and provides a cushioning effect. They are commonly used in applications where a secure fit is needed, such as in fastening bolts or screws to prevent damage to surfaces or to retain a certain tension.","nf":8},{"id":"590","name":"Hinge Rings","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":12,"img":"img/590.png","desc":"Hinge rings are circular fasteners designed to connect two components, allowing them to pivot or rotate around a central axis, similar to a hinge. They are commonly used in applications such as doors, gates, and machinery, providing a simple and durable solution for rotational movement.","nf":0},{"id":"1230","name":"Offset Washer","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":6,"img":"img/1230.png","desc":"An offset washer is a type of washer designed with an eccentric shape, featuring a hole that is slightly off-center to create a controlled gap or offset between a fastener and the surface it is attached to. It is often used to correct alignment issues, distribute load unevenly, or compensate for slight variations in hole size.","nf":4},{"id":"1271","name":"Finger Spring Washer","path":"Fasteners > Washers","n":5,"img":"img/1271.png","desc":"A finger spring washer is a type of elastic washer designed with multiple curved \"fingers\" that provide a spring-like force to maintain tension and prevent loosening of fasteners. It is commonly used in assemblies where vibration or movement could cause bolts or screws to loosen over time.","nf":1}]},{"name":"Vented Fasteners","n":6816,"img":"img/1296.png","kids":[{"name":"Vented Screws","n":6776,"img":"img/1296.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1296","name":"Vented Socket Head Cap Screws","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Screws","n":4821,"img":"img/1296.png","desc":"Vented socket head cap screws are fasteners with an internal hexagonal drive and a vented or drilled hole in the head, designed to allow the release of pressure or gases from the assembly. They are commonly used in applications where air or fluid circulation is needed, such as in high-performance machinery or systems with high internal pressure.","nf":16},{"id":"1297","name":"Vented Flat Head Socket Screws","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Screws","n":771,"img":"img/1297.png","desc":"Vented flat head socket screws are fasteners with a flat, countersunk head and a hole or vent in the center, designed to allow gases or liquids to escape during installation. They are commonly used in applications where pressure buildup or fluid leakage needs to be managed, such as in automotive or industrial machinery.","nf":17},{"id":"1295","name":"Vented Button Head Socket Screws","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Screws","n":511,"img":"img/1295.png","desc":"Vented button head socket screws are fasteners with a low-profile, rounded head and a small vent hole designed to allow airflow or release pressure in certain applications. They are commonly used in situations where space is limited and venting is required, such as in electronics or high-performance machinery.","nf":17},{"id":"1299","name":"Vented Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Screws","n":418,"img":"img/1299.png","desc":"Vented set screws are fasteners with a hole or vent in the body that allows gases, fluids, or pressure to escape when the screw is installed. They are commonly used in applications where controlling fluid or air flow is necessary, such as in hydraulic or pneumatic systems.","nf":11},{"id":"1309","name":"Vented Hex Cap Screws","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Screws","n":106,"img":"img/1309.png","desc":"Vented hex cap screws are fasteners with a hexagonal head and a vent or hole in the shaft, designed to allow gases, liquids, or pressure to escape during installation. They are commonly used in applications where managing fluid or air flow is important, such as in hydraulic or pneumatic systems.","nf":16},{"id":"1298","name":"Vented Machine Screws","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Screws","n":99,"img":"img/1298.png","desc":"A vented machine screw is a type of fastener that features a small hole or vent in the shaft or head, allowing for the release of gases or pressure in certain applications. These screws are commonly used in environments where heat, pressure, or fluid buildup needs to be managed, such as in automotive or industrial systems.","nf":9},{"id":"1310","name":"Vented Shoulder Screws","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Screws","n":50,"img":"img/1310.png","desc":"Vented shoulder screws are specialized fasteners with a shoulder section that allows for alignment and support, featuring holes or vents designed to permit the passage of air, gases, or fluids. These screws are commonly used in applications where pressure release or fluid drainage is required, such as in machinery or automotive systems.","nf":8}]},{"name":"Vented Washers","n":31,"img":"img/1301.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1301","name":"Vented Flat Washers","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Washers","n":31,"img":"img/1301.png","desc":"Vented flat washers are washers designed with small holes or slots to allow for the passage of air, water, or other fluids, preventing the buildup of pressure or moisture. They are commonly used in applications where drainage or ventilation is needed, such as in automotive or plumbing systems.","nf":3}]},{"name":"Vented Nuts","n":9,"img":"img/1303.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1303","name":"Vented Hex Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Vented Fasteners > Vented Nuts","n":9,"img":"img/1303.png","desc":"Vented hex nuts are hexagonal-shaped fasteners with small vents or holes designed to allow air or gas to escape during tightening, preventing pressure buildup. They are often used in applications where components need to be sealed without trapping moisture, air, or other gases, such as in high-pressure systems or electronics.","nf":4}]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Nuts","n":5219,"img":"img/170.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"170","name":"Hex Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":1488,"img":"img/170.png","desc":"A hex nut is a six-sided fastener used to secure bolts, rods, or screws by threading onto the male threads of these components. It is widely used in mechanical, automotive, and construction applications due to its versatility and strength.","nf":12},{"id":"174","name":"Lock Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":1234,"img":"img/174.png","desc":"Lock nuts are specialized fasteners designed to prevent loosening due to vibration or movement by incorporating a mechanism that resists rotational forces. They are commonly used in mechanical applications to ensure the secure fastening of bolts and screws.","nf":17},{"id":"171","name":"Jam Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":524,"img":"img/171.png","desc":"Jam nuts are thin, hexagonal nuts used alongside a regular nut to secure and lock it in place, preventing it from loosening due to vibration or movement. They are commonly employed in mechanical and automotive applications, providing additional security to threaded connections.","nf":11},{"id":"939","name":"Heavy Hex Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":382,"img":"img/939.png","desc":"A heavy hex nut is a type of hex nut that is thicker and stronger than standard hex nuts, providing greater durability and resistance to high-stress applications. It is commonly used in heavy-duty industries such as construction, machinery, and structural connections where added strength is required.","nf":10},{"id":"184","name":"Weld Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":241,"img":"img/184.png","desc":"Weld nuts are specialized fasteners designed to be welded onto a surface to provide a threaded connection for bolts or screws. They are commonly used in applications where a strong, permanent attachment point is needed without the need for a separate nut.","nf":9},{"id":"168","name":"Flange Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":222,"img":"img/168.png","desc":"Flange nuts are a type of nut that features a built-in, wider base (flange) that acts as a washer, distributing the load and reducing the risk of damage to the surface. They are commonly used in applications where space constraints or a need for additional stability and security exist.","nf":15},{"id":"162","name":"Acorn Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":220,"img":"img/162.png","desc":"Acorn nuts are hexagonal nuts with a domed, closed end that covers the exposed threads of a bolt, providing a smooth, protective finish. They are commonly used to prevent damage to the threads and to enhance safety by covering sharp edges.","nf":11},{"id":"181","name":"Tee Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":145,"img":"img/181.png","desc":"Tee nuts are fasteners with a cylindrical body and pronged ends designed to be inserted into wood or soft materials, providing a secure threaded insert for bolts. They are commonly used in furniture construction, cabinetry, and mechanical assemblies to create a strong, reliable connection.","nf":10},{"id":"185","name":"Wing Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":120,"img":"img/185.png","desc":"Wing nuts are fasteners with two large \"wings\" on either side, allowing for easy hand tightening and loosening without the need for tools. They are typically used in applications where quick adjustments or frequent disassembly are required.","nf":9},{"id":"177","name":"Slotted and Bearing Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":89,"img":"img/177.png","desc":"Slotted nuts are fasteners with a vertical slot or grooves that allow for easy installation and removal using a screwdriver or similar tool, typically paired with a cotter pin to prevent loosening. Bearing nuts are designed with a bearing surface to reduce friction and wear, often used in assemblies where rotation or movement is involved.","nf":9},{"id":"166","name":"Coupling Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":81,"img":"img/166.png","desc":"Coupling nuts are cylindrical fasteners with internal threads at both ends, designed to connect and extend the length of two externally threaded components. They are commonly used in mechanical and construction applications to join threaded rods, pipes, or bolts securely.","nf":10},{"id":"179","name":"Square Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":77,"img":"img/179.png","desc":"Square nuts are nuts with a square-shaped body, offering more surface area for a better grip when fastening. They are often used in applications requiring higher torque or in conjunction with square bolts to prevent rotation.","nf":9},{"id":"1324","name":"Heavy Hex Jam Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":74,"img":"","desc":"","nf":7},{"id":"943","name":"Keps and K-Lock Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":72,"img":"img/943.png","desc":"Keps and K-lock nuts are fasteners that combine a nut with an integrated external tooth lock washer, providing resistance against loosening due to vibration. They are commonly used in applications requiring secure fastening, where both the nut and washer functions are needed in one convenient component.","nf":12},{"id":"165","name":"Castle Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":65,"img":"img/165.png","desc":"Castle nuts are hexagonal nuts with a notched, castellated outer surface, designed to be used with a cotter pin to prevent loosening from vibration or movement. They are commonly used in automotive, machinery, and aerospace applications to secure critical components.","nf":13},{"id":"172","name":"Knurled Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":46,"img":"img/172.png","desc":"Knurled nuts are nuts with a textured, patterned surface designed to improve grip and allow for easier manual tightening and loosening. They are commonly used in applications where hand adjustment is needed without the use of tools.","nf":10},{"id":"167","name":"Electrical Panel Nut","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":44,"img":"img/167.png","desc":"An electrical panel nut is a type of fastener used to secure components, such as circuit breakers or terminals, within an electrical panel. These nuts are designed to ensure a tight, secure connection, preventing loosening or disconnection that could lead to electrical faults or hazards.","nf":7},{"id":"163","name":"Cage Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":29,"img":"img/163.png","desc":"Cage nuts are fasteners designed to be inserted into a metal rack or enclosure, allowing for easy attachment of equipment or panels. They consist of a nut encased in a metal cage, which helps secure the nut in place and prevent it from spinning during installation.","nf":6},{"id":"176","name":"Palnuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":28,"img":"img/176.png","desc":"Palnuts are a type of spring steel lock washer used to prevent bolts and nuts from loosening due to vibrations or torque. They have a unique, bent shape that exerts pressure on the fastener, creating a secure, vibration-resistant connection.","nf":6},{"id":"178","name":"Spring Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":23,"img":"img/178.png","desc":"Spring nuts are specialized fasteners that feature a spring-like design, allowing them to provide a tight, secure grip on threaded rods or bolts. They are often used in applications where vibration or movement could cause traditional nuts to loosen, offering a reliable, self-locking solution.","nf":5},{"id":"182","name":"Thumb Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Nuts","n":15,"img":"img/182.png","desc":"Thumb nuts are small, knurled nuts that can be easily tightened or loosened by hand, without the need for tools. They are commonly used in applications where frequent adjustments are needed, such as in equipment assemblies, where convenience and quick fastening are required.","nf":8}]},{"name":"Set Screws","n":4668,"img":"img/998.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"998","name":"Cup Point Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":1730,"img":"img/998.png","desc":"A cup point set screw is a type of fastener with a rounded, cup-shaped tip designed to provide a secure, tight grip on the surface it contacts. It is commonly used to prevent movement or slippage in mechanical assemblies, such as securing gears or pulleys to shafts.","nf":12},{"id":"999","name":"Flat Point Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":730,"img":"img/999.png","desc":"A flat point set screw is a type of fastener with a flat, flat-tipped end designed to sit flush against the surface it contacts. It is commonly used to secure components in place without causing damage to softer materials, providing a firm grip while offering minimal protrusion.","nf":11},{"id":"568","name":"Square Head Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":495,"img":"img/568.png","desc":"A square head set screw is a type of fastener with a square-shaped head that provides a better grip for tools, making it easier to tighten or loosen in confined spaces. It is commonly used in mechanical and industrial applications where high torque is required, ensuring a secure and reliable hold.","nf":12},{"id":"996","name":"Brass Tip Set Screw","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":319,"img":"img/996.png","desc":"A brass tip set screw is a type of fastener with a brass tip designed to prevent damage or wear on the surface it contacts, such as delicate or soft materials. It is commonly used in mechanical assemblies where a secure hold is needed without marring the component being fastened, such as in machinery, electronics, or musical instruments.","nf":12},{"id":"1002","name":"Oval Point Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":257,"img":"img/1002.png","desc":"Oval point set screws are fasteners with a rounded, oval-shaped tip designed to make contact with a surface without causing significant damage. They are commonly used to secure components in place, offering a more even distribution of pressure compared to flat or pointed set screws.","nf":11},{"id":"1243","name":"Knurled Point","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":253,"img":"img/1243.png","desc":"A knurled point is a type of set screw with a textured, patterned tip that enhances grip and prevents slipping when applied to a surface. It is commonly used in applications where a strong, non-marring hold is required, such as in fastening delicate or soft materials.","nf":9},{"id":"997","name":"Cone Point Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":231,"img":"img/997.png","desc":"Cone point set screws are fasteners with a conically shaped tip that provides a strong, concentrated grip on the surface it contacts. They are commonly used in mechanical applications to securely fasten components, such as gears or pulleys, onto shafts without causing significant damage.","nf":10},{"id":"1242","name":"Slotted Set Screw","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":203,"img":"img/1242.png","desc":"A slotted set screw is a type of fastener with a flat tip and a single slot on the head, designed to be tightened or loosened with a flathead screwdriver. It is commonly used to secure components in place, especially in mechanical assemblies where precise adjustment is needed.","nf":15},{"id":"1244","name":"Half Dog Set Screw","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":185,"img":"img/1244.png","desc":"A half dog set screw is a type of fastener with a flat or pointed tip, designed to secure components onto a shaft or in a specific position without fully threading into the material. It features a partially threaded shaft and is commonly used in mechanical applications where a secure hold is needed without damaging the surface of the part being fastened.","nf":12},{"id":"1000","name":"Full Dog Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":160,"img":"img/1000.png","desc":"Full dog set screws are fasteners with a pointed tip and a collar that extends around the shaft, providing a secure grip without damaging the surface. They are commonly used in mechanical applications to hold components in place, especially when a strong and permanent hold is needed.","nf":11},{"id":"1245","name":"Socket Set Screws Misc...","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":79,"img":"img/1245.png","desc":"Socket set screws are small, fully threaded fasteners with a recessed hexagonal drive that are typically used to secure one part to another, such as in shafts or collars. They come in various types, including plain, cup point, or flat point, and are commonly used in machinery and mechanical assemblies where precision and a strong hold are required.","nf":9},{"id":"565","name":"Hex Head Set Screws","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":15,"img":"img/565.png","desc":"Hex head set screws are fasteners with a hexagonal-shaped head and a fully threaded shaft, designed to secure objects in place by being screwed into a hole or against a surface. They are commonly used in mechanical and automotive applications where a strong, reliable connection is needed to prevent movement or slippage.","nf":8},{"id":"1003","name":"Partial Thread Set Screw","path":"Fasteners > Set Screws","n":11,"img":"img/1003.png","desc":"A partial thread set screw is a fastener with threading that only extends partway along its length, designed to secure components without fully passing through the material. It is commonly used in applications where a portion of the screw remains unthreaded, such as in locking mechanisms or when adjusting the position of a part.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Pins","n":4215,"img":"img/507.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"507","name":"Dowel Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":1723,"img":"img/507.png","desc":"Dowel pins are cylindrical rods used to align and join two or more pieces of material, typically wood or metal, by fitting into corresponding holes. They provide a precise, strong connection and are commonly used in woodworking, furniture making, and machinery to ensure accurate positioning and stability.","nf":12},{"id":"514","name":"Spring Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":906,"img":"img/514.png","desc":"Spring pins are cylindrical fasteners made of spring steel, designed to be inserted into a hole to secure components in place while allowing for some flexibility. They are commonly used in machinery and automotive applications for quick and reliable assembly, providing a strong yet removable connection.","nf":10},{"id":"515","name":"Taper Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":572,"img":"img/515.png","desc":"Taper pins are cylindrical fasteners with a tapered shape, designed to fit into matching tapered holes to create a strong, secure connection. As they are driven into the hole, the taper creates a tight fit, preventing axial movement and providing a reliable bond in various mechanical applications.","nf":3},{"id":"506","name":"Cotter Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":405,"img":"img/506.png","desc":"Cotter pins are fasteners used to secure other components in place by passing through a hole and then bending the ends to prevent the pin from slipping out. They are commonly used in machinery, automotive, and agricultural applications to keep parts like bolts and nuts securely fastened.","nf":8},{"id":"505","name":"Clevis Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":197,"img":"img/505.png","desc":"Clevis pins are cylindrical fasteners with a hole at one end, designed to be inserted into a clevis and secured with a cotter pin or retaining clip. They are commonly used in mechanical linkages and suspension systems to connect components while allowing for rotational movement.","nf":12},{"id":"508","name":"Groove Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":187,"img":"img/508.png","desc":"Groove pins are cylindrical fastening components with grooves along their surface, designed to hold components in place by providing a secure grip when inserted into a hole. The grooves allow the pin to resist rotation and prevent it from slipping out, making it ideal for applications that require a strong, permanent fixation.","nf":7},{"id":"1316","name":"Hairpin Cotter Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":79,"img":"img/1316.png","desc":"Hairpin cotter pins are a type of fastener shaped like a \"U\" or hairpin, designed to secure components on shafts or pins by passing through a hole and then bending the ends to hold them in place. They are commonly used in mechanical and automotive applications to prevent parts from sliding out of position or becoming dislodged.","nf":4},{"id":"1306","name":"Pivot Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":76,"img":"img/1306.png","desc":"Pivot pins are cylindrical fasteners used to create a rotating or swiveling connection between two components, allowing for controlled movement. They are commonly found in mechanical systems, such as machinery or vehicles, where parts need to rotate or pivot around a fixed point.","nf":4},{"id":"511","name":"Linch Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":27,"img":"img/511.png","desc":"Linch pins are simple fastening devices used to secure components or parts in place by inserting them into a hole and locking them with a spring-loaded mechanism. Commonly used in machinery, trailers, and agricultural equipment, they prevent accidental detachment while allowing for quick removal when needed.","nf":6},{"id":"516","name":"Weld Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":24,"img":"img/516.png","desc":"Weld pins are fasteners used in various welding applications to secure materials together by creating a strong bond through a welding process. They are typically used in industries such as HVAC and automotive for attaching insulation, lining, or other components to metal surfaces.","nf":5},{"id":"957","name":"Split Rings","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":10,"img":"img/957.png","desc":"Split rings are circular metal rings with a gap or slit, allowing them to be opened and easily attached or removed from a component. They are commonly used in applications like keychains, electrical connections, or mechanical assemblies to secure parts without requiring additional fasteners.","nf":0},{"id":"512","name":"Snap/Tab Lock Pins","path":"Fasteners > Pins","n":9,"img":"img/512.png","desc":"Snap/Tab Lock Pins are mechanical fasteners that use a spring-loaded pin with a tab or snap mechanism to securely lock components in place. They are typically used for quick-release or adjustable applications, providing a reliable and simple method for joining parts.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Rods and Studs","n":2237,"img":"img/540.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"540","name":"Fully Threaded Studs","path":"Fasteners > Rods and Studs","n":1243,"img":"img/540.png","desc":"Fully threaded studs are fasteners with continuous threading along their entire length, designed to be inserted into pre-drilled holes or used with nuts to secure components together. They are commonly used in applications requiring strong, durable connections and are especially useful for joining parts where both ends need to be fastened.","nf":9},{"id":"542","name":"Threaded Rods","path":"Fasteners > Rods and Studs","n":595,"img":"img/542.png","desc":"Threaded rods are long, cylindrical fasteners with continuous threading along their entire length, designed to be used with nuts or to be cut to specific sizes for various applications. They are commonly used in construction, mechanical, and industrial applications to connect or support components with high tensile strength.","nf":11},{"id":"539","name":"Double End Studs","path":"Fasteners > Rods and Studs","n":250,"img":"img/539.png","desc":"Double end studs are threaded fasteners that feature threads on both ends, allowing for a secure connection between two parts. They are commonly used in applications where two components need to be joined or adjusted, with each end being inserted into a different part for stability.","nf":9},{"id":"543","name":"Threaded Studs","path":"Fasteners > Rods and Studs","n":113,"img":"img/543.png","desc":"Threaded studs are fasteners with threads along their entire length, designed to be inserted into a hole or a nut to create a strong, secure connection. They are commonly used in mechanical, automotive, and construction applications where a permanent or adjustable fastening solution is required.","nf":9},{"id":"1325","name":"Stud Misc","path":"Fasteners > Rods and Studs","n":15,"img":"","desc":"","nf":3},{"id":"544","name":"Weld Studs","path":"Fasteners > Rods and Studs","n":14,"img":"img/544.png","desc":"Weld studs are metal fasteners designed to be attached to a surface through welding, creating a strong, permanent bond. They are commonly used in applications like automotive and construction, where components need to be securely anchored without drilling or threading.","nf":7},{"id":"541","name":"Single End Stud","path":"Fasteners > Rods and Studs","n":7,"img":"img/541.png","desc":"A single end stud is a threaded fastener with threads on only one end, typically used to secure components by screwing into a threaded hole while the other end remains unthreaded for attachment to a nut or other fitting. It is commonly used in applications such as automotive, machinery, and construction where a fixed attachment point is required.","nf":6}]},{"name":"Rivets","n":1780,"img":"img/526.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"526","name":"Blind Rivets","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":1032,"img":"img/526.png","desc":"Blind rivets are a type of fastener that can be installed from one side of a workpiece, making them ideal for applications where access to the opposite side is limited. They consist of a rivet body and a mandrel, which is pulled to expand the rivet and create a secure, permanent joint.","nf":25},{"id":"531","name":"Rivet Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":236,"img":"img/531.png","desc":"Rivet nuts are fasteners that provide a threaded insert in thin or hollow materials, allowing for a secure attachment of bolts or screws. They are installed by inserting them into a pre-drilled hole and then expanding them using a tool to create a strong, permanent thread.","nf":10},{"id":"536","name":"Solid Rivets","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":167,"img":"img/536.png","desc":"Solid rivets are permanent mechanical fasteners that consist of a cylindrical shaft and a head, used to join two or more materials together. When installed, the shaft is deformed, forming a second head on the opposite side, creating a secure and durable bond that resists vibration and shear forces.","nf":7},{"id":"1203","name":"Rivet Tool Products","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":98,"img":"img/1203.png","desc":"Rivet tool products are specialized tools used to insert and secure rivets, which are permanent fasteners used to join materials together. These tools, which include hand riveters, pneumatic, and hydraulic rivet guns, are commonly used in industries such as construction, automotive, and aerospace for creating strong, durable connections.","nf":1},{"id":"535","name":"Semi-Tubular Rivets","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":82,"img":"img/535.png","desc":"Semi-tubular rivets are fasteners with a partially hollow shaft that allows for easier deformation during installation, creating a strong, permanent connection between materials. They are commonly used in applications where a lightweight, secure fastening solution is required, such as in electronics, automotive, and furniture manufacturing.","nf":4},{"id":"1288","name":"Rivet Miscell...","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":64,"img":"img/1288.png","desc":"Rivet miscellaneous (misc.) refers to a collection of various rivet types and related components used for fastening materials together in a wide range of applications. These can include different sizes, materials, and styles of rivets, as well as related tools and accessories, suited for tasks in manufacturing, construction, and repair work.","nf":4},{"id":"528","name":"Rivet Back-Up Washer","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":23,"img":"img/528.png","desc":"A rivet back-up washer is a type of washer used behind a rivet to distribute the load and prevent damage to the material being fastened. It helps ensure a secure and stable connection by providing additional support and minimizing the risk of the rivet pulling through or causing deformation.","nf":3},{"id":"534","name":"Self Piercing Rivets","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":22,"img":"img/534.png","desc":"Self-piercing rivets are a type of fastener designed to join materials by piercing through one or more layers without the need for pre-drilled holes. These rivets create a strong, permanent bond by deforming the rivet material as it penetrates the workpieces, making them ideal for sheet metal applications.","nf":2},{"id":"530","name":"Rivet Lock Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":20,"img":"img/530.png","desc":"Rivet lock bolts are fasteners that combine the features of a rivet and a bolt, designed to provide a secure, permanent connection by locking into place once installed. They are commonly used in structural applications, such as aerospace or heavy machinery, where a strong, vibration-resistant fastening solution is needed","nf":9},{"id":"1328","name":"Insert Tool","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":19,"img":"","desc":"","nf":0},{"id":"529","name":"Rivet Collars","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":10,"img":"img/529.png","desc":"Rivet collars are circular components that are used in conjunction with rivets to secure and fasten two or more materials together. They help distribute the load evenly and provide additional support, ensuring a strong and durable connection in applications such as sheet metal assembly or aircraft construction.","nf":0},{"id":"974","name":"Shoulder Rivet","path":"Fasteners > Rivets","n":7,"img":"img/974.png","desc":"A shoulder rivet is a type of mechanical fastener with a cylindrical shoulder that provides a precise and stable connection between two components. It is commonly used in applications where a load-bearing, non-rotating, and secure attachment is required, such as in automotive, aerospace, or machinery assembly.","nf":3}]},{"name":"Retaining Rings and Clips","n":1228,"img":"img/520.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"520","name":"External Retaining Rings","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":457,"img":"img/520.png","desc":"External retaining rings are circular fasteners designed to fit around the outer circumference of a shaft or housing, holding components in place within a mechanical assembly. They are commonly used in applications where space is limited, providing a secure and reliable method of retaining parts without the need for additional hardware.","nf":11},{"id":"517","name":"E-Clips","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":223,"img":"img/517.png","desc":"E-clips are small, circular retaining clips with an \"E\" shape, designed to fit into grooves on shafts or pins to secure components in place. They are commonly used in mechanical assemblies, such as automotive and industrial machinery, to prevent parts from sliding or coming loose.","nf":9},{"id":"518","name":"Internal Retaining Rings","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":220,"img":"img/518.png","desc":"Internal retaining rings are circular fasteners designed to fit inside a bore or housing to hold components in place, preventing them from sliding or falling out. They are installed in a groove within the bore and provide secure, reliable retention in various mechanical and industrial applications.","nf":10},{"id":"519","name":"Spiral Rings","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":132,"img":"img/519.png","desc":"Spiral rings are circular fasteners with a continuous coil design, often used to retain components on shafts or in housings, preventing them from slipping out of position. They are commonly used in mechanical assemblies where secure retention is needed without requiring additional fasteners, such as in automotive, industrial, and electrical applications.","nf":9},{"id":"1241","name":"Retaining Rings MISC..","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":88,"img":"img/1241.png","desc":"Retaining rings miscellaneous (MISC.) refers to a variety of retaining rings and associated components used to secure parts in place within mechanical assemblies. These rings can come in different shapes, sizes, and materials, and are commonly used in automotive, industrial, and machinery applications to prevent axial movement of components like bearings or shafts.","nf":5},{"id":"960","name":"External Push Ring","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":58,"img":"img/960.png","desc":"An external push ring is a type of retaining ring designed to fit around the outside of a shaft or housing, holding components in place by applying outward pressure. It is commonly used in mechanical assemblies to prevent parts from sliding off or becoming dislodged while allowing for easy installation and removal.","nf":8},{"id":"965","name":"Sealing Retaining Rings","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":37,"img":"img/965.png","desc":"Sealing retaining rings are circular fasteners designed to secure components in place while also providing a seal to prevent leakage of fluids or gases. They are commonly used in machinery, automotive, and hydraulic systems to maintain pressure and prevent contaminants from entering or escaping.","nf":6},{"id":"966","name":"U-Clips","path":"Fasteners > Retaining Rings and Clips","n":13,"img":"img/966.png","desc":"U-clips are U-shaped metal fasteners used to secure components or parts, typically by clipping them into a slot or groove. They are commonly used in automotive, electrical, and construction applications for fastening wiring, panels, or trim without the need for additional tools.","nf":1}]},{"name":"Clinch Fasteners","n":944,"img":"img/209.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"209","name":"Self Clinching Standoffs","path":"Fasteners > Clinch Fasteners","n":346,"img":"img/209.png","desc":"Self-clinching standoffs are fasteners designed to create a secure, permanent raised connection in thin sheet metal, allowing for the mounting of components. When pressed into a pre-drilled hole, the standoff clinches onto the material, providing a stable, threaded attachment point without the need for additional hardware.","nf":5},{"id":"208","name":"Self Clinching Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Clinch Fasteners","n":301,"img":"img/208.png","desc":"Self-clinching nuts are fasteners that provide a strong, permanent threaded connection in thin sheet metal without the need for welding or additional fastening hardware. When pressed into a pre-drilled hole, the nut's design causes it to clinch onto the material, creating a secure, flush-fit attachment.","nf":7},{"id":"210","name":"Self Clinching Studs","path":"Fasteners > Clinch Fasteners","n":297,"img":"img/210.png","desc":"Self-clinching studs are fasteners designed to be permanently attached to thin metal sheets or panels without the need for welding or additional hardware. They feature a tapered shank that, when pressed into a pre-drilled hole, deforms the material to create a secure, threaded connection.","nf":9}]},{"name":"Automotive Fasteners","n":770,"img":"img/26.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"26","name":"Push Nut Retainers","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":286,"img":"img/26.png","desc":"Push nut retainers are small, circular fasteners designed to secure components on a shaft or rod by pressing onto the shaft and locking into place without the need for threading. They are commonly used in applications like automotive or machinery to hold parts firmly and prevent them from slipping or becoming dislodge","nf":6},{"id":"1095","name":"Retainers","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":110,"img":"img/1095.png","desc":"Retainers are mechanical components designed to hold or secure parts in place, preventing them from moving or becoming dislodged during operation. They are used in a variety of applications, including automotive, machinery, and construction, to ensure stability and safety of connected components.","nf":5},{"id":"22","name":"Automotive Bumpers","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":90,"img":"img/22.png","desc":"Automotive bumpers are protective structures mounted on the front and rear of vehicles to absorb impact during collisions and minimize damage to the vehicle's body. They are typically made from durable materials like steel, aluminum, or plastic and are designed to meet safety regulations while contributing to the vehicle's overall appearance.","nf":4},{"id":"1097","name":"U Nut","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":80,"img":"img/1097.png","desc":"A U nut is a type of fastener with a U-shaped design, typically used to secure components to a surface, often providing a secure grip on thin or soft materials. It is commonly used in applications where a quick, reliable attachment is needed, such as in automotive, electronic, and furniture assembly.","nf":9},{"id":"1238","name":"Wheel Nut","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":50,"img":"img/1238.png","desc":"A wheel nut (or lug nut) is a type of fastener used to secure a wheel onto a vehicle's axle by threading onto the corresponding lug bolts or studs. It is essential for ensuring the safe attachment of the wheel, with variations in size and design depending on the vehicle type and intended load capacity.","nf":11},{"id":"1099","name":"Wheel Stud","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":41,"img":"img/1099.png","desc":"A wheel stud is a threaded fastener used to secure a wheel to a vehicle, typically through a lug nut. It is installed into the wheel hub and provides a strong, reliable connection between the wheel and the axle, ensuring proper alignment and safety.","nf":10},{"id":"28","name":"Automotive Fasteners Misc..","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":39,"img":"img/28.png","desc":"Automotive fasteners are a wide range of components used to secure, assemble, and hold various parts of a vehicle together, including bolts, nuts, screws, clips, and rivets. These fasteners are specifically designed to withstand the demanding conditions of automotive environments, such as vibration, heat, and corrosion.","nf":9},{"id":"25","name":"Automotive Plugs","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":36,"img":"img/25.png","desc":"Automotive plugs are electrical connectors used in vehicles to establish a secure connection between wires and components, such as sensors, lights, or ignition systems. They are designed to withstand high temperatures, vibrations, and harsh environments, ensuring reliable performance in automotive applications.","nf":8},{"id":"1237","name":"Well Nut","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":19,"img":"img/1237.png","desc":"A well nut is a type of fastener that consists of a rubber insert with a metal insert or sleeve, designed to expand when a bolt is tightened. It is commonly used to secure components in applications where a vibration-resistant and watertight seal is needed, such as in automotive or plumbing systems.","nf":13},{"id":"1263","name":"Wheel Weights","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":11,"img":"img/1263.png","desc":"Wheel weights are small metal pieces attached to the rims of wheels to balance them and ensure smooth rotation. They are typically used in automotive and industrial applications to prevent vibrations and improve vehicle stability by compensating for uneven weight distribution.","nf":1},{"id":"1104","name":"Bungee Straps","path":"Fasteners > Automotive Fasteners","n":8,"img":"img/1104.png","desc":"Bungee straps are elastic cords with hooks at each end, designed to secure items by stretching and providing tension. They are commonly used in outdoor, transportation, and storage applications to hold down cargo or bundle objects together.","nf":7}]},{"name":"Anchors","n":702,"img":"img/19.png","kids":[{"name":"Anchor Installation","n":50,"img":"img/1200.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1200","name":"Anchoring Tools","path":"Fasteners > Anchors > Anchor Installation","n":38,"img":"img/1200.png","desc":"Anchoring tools are devices used to secure or fasten objects to a surface or substrate, ensuring stability and preventing movement. They are commonly used in construction, marine, and automotive applications to provide a reliable anchor point for heavy equipment, structures, or cables.","nf":0},{"id":"1202","name":"Nozzles","path":"Fasteners > Anchors > Anchor Installation","n":12,"img":"img/1202.png","desc":"Nozzles are devices used to control the flow, direction, or characteristics of a fluid or gas as it exits a pipe or container. They are commonly employed in various industries, including automotive, agriculture, and manufacturing, to direct or modify the pressure and velocity of the flow for specific applications.","nf":0}]}],"cats":[{"id":"19","name":"Wall Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":197,"img":"img/19.png","desc":"Wall anchors are fastening devices used to secure screws or bolts into walls, providing a strong hold in materials such as drywall, plaster, or masonry. They expand or grip the surrounding material as the screw is driven in, preventing the anchor from pulling out and ensuring a secure attachment for fixtures or hardware.","nf":8},{"id":"20","name":"Wedge Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":171,"img":"img/20.png","desc":"Wedge anchors are heavy-duty fasteners designed for securing objects to concrete or masonry surfaces. They feature a tapered, wedge-shaped end that expands as the bolt is tightened, providing a strong, reliable hold in the material.","nf":6},{"id":"15","name":"Sleeve Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":126,"img":"img/15.png","desc":"Sleeve anchors are fasteners designed for anchoring objects to concrete, brick, or masonry by expanding within the hole as the screw is tightened. They provide a strong, reliable hold and are commonly used in construction and heavy-duty applications to secure fixtures or equipment.","nf":10},{"id":"11","name":"Drop-In Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":41,"img":"img/11.png","desc":"Drop-in anchors are fasteners used to provide a secure, flush-mount threaded anchor point in concrete or masonry surfaces. They are designed to be inserted into pre-drilled holes and then expanded using a setting tool, providing a strong and stable anchor for bolts or other attachments.","nf":6},{"id":"1322","name":"Adhesives","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":38,"img":"","desc":"","nf":0},{"id":"12","name":"Expansion Shield Anchor","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":16,"img":"img/12.png","desc":"An expansion shield anchor is a type of fastener used to secure bolts or screws into masonry or concrete by expanding against the sides of a pre-drilled hole. As the bolt is tightened, the anchor expands, creating a strong and stable grip within the material for reliable fastening.","nf":1},{"id":"9","name":"Drive Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":13,"img":"img/9.png","desc":"Drive anchors are fasteners designed to be driven into materials like concrete, brick, or masonry to provide a secure hold for screws or bolts. They expand as they are driven in, creating a tight grip that ensures stability and prevents loosening in construction and industrial applications.","nf":1},{"id":"16","name":"Stud Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":12,"img":"img/16.png","desc":"Stud anchors are fasteners that feature a threaded stud and are used to secure components or structures to a surface, typically in concrete or masonry. They are commonly used in construction, automotive, and industrial applications for providing a strong, permanent attachment point for various parts or equipment.","nf":4},{"id":"17","name":"T-Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":12,"img":"img/17.png","desc":"T-anchors are specialized fastening devices designed to provide a secure attachment point by embedding into concrete, wood, or masonry, with a T-shaped body that resists pull-out forces. They are commonly used in applications where a strong, permanent anchor is needed for heavy-duty loads or structural support","nf":1},{"id":"8","name":"Chemical Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":12,"img":"img/8.png","desc":"Chemical anchors are fastening systems that use a resin or adhesive to bond and secure a threaded rod or rebar into a substrate, such as concrete or masonry. They provide strong, reliable anchors in applications where traditional mechanical anchors may not be suitable, particularly in cracked or brittle materials.","nf":1},{"id":"6","name":"Bent Anchor Bolts","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":4,"img":"img/6.png","desc":"Bent anchor bolts are heavy-duty fasteners designed to secure structures to concrete or masonry, featuring a bent or curved shape at one end for better grip and stability. They are commonly used in construction and industrial applications to anchor beams, columns, and machinery to foundations.","nf":2},{"id":"1235","name":"Universal Drive Pin Rivet","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":3,"img":"img/1235.png","desc":"A universal drive pin rivet is a type of fastener used to join materials together, featuring a pin that is driven into the rivet body to create a permanent, secure hold. It is versatile, typically used in automotive, construction, and manufacturing applications for its ability to work with a variety of materials and provide strong, reliable fastening.","nf":0},{"id":"7","name":"Bolt Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":3,"img":"img/7.png","desc":"A bolt anchor is a fastening device used to secure an object to a surface by embedding a bolt into a pre-drilled hole, typically in concrete or masonry. It expands or tightens within the hole, providing a strong, durable hold for heavy loads or equipment.","nf":2},{"id":"13","name":"Expansion Bolt","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":2,"img":"img/13.png","desc":"An expansion bolt is a type of anchor fastener used to secure objects to solid materials like concrete or brick. It expands upon installation, creating a tight, secure fit within the hole, providing a strong and reliable attachment point for heavy-duty applications.","nf":1},{"id":"18","name":"Umbrella Anchors","path":"Fasteners > Anchors","n":2,"img":"img/18.png","desc":"Umbrella anchors are a type of anchoring device used to secure objects or structures to the ground, featuring a design that expands like an umbrella when deployed. They are commonly used in marine, construction, and heavy-duty applications for their ability to provide strong, reliable hold in various soil or surface conditions.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Furniture Fasteners","n":67,"img":"img/211.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"211","name":"Joint Connector Bolt","path":"Fasteners > Furniture Fasteners","n":54,"img":"img/211.png","desc":"A joint connector bolt is a fastener used to securely join two or more components, typically in construction or machinery, by passing through pre-drilled holes. It ensures a stable and reliable connection, distributing load and providing strength to the assembled parts.","nf":11},{"id":"212","name":"Joint Connector Nuts","path":"Fasteners > Furniture Fasteners","n":13,"img":"img/212.png","desc":"Joint connector nuts are fasteners used to join two components together by threading onto their respective bolts or studs, ensuring a secure and stable connection. They are commonly used in applications such as furniture assembly, construction, and machinery to align and hold parts firmly in place.","nf":6}]}],"cats":[{"id":"63","name":"Threaded Inserts","path":"Fasteners","n":748,"img":"img/63.png","desc":"Threaded inserts are cylindrical components with internal threads that are used to provide a durable, wear-resistant threaded hole in softer materials like wood or plastic. They allow for repeated assembly and disassembly of screws or bolts without damaging the base material.","nf":9}]},{"name":"Hardware","n":6039,"img":"img/50.png","kids":[{"name":"Electronic Hardware","n":2299,"img":"img/1283.png","kids":[{"name":"Standoffs","n":1508,"img":"img/1283.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1283","name":"Male-Female Standoffs","path":"Hardware > Electronic Hardware > Standoffs","n":1207,"img":"img/1283.png","desc":"Male-female standoffs are cylindrical connectors with a male thread on one end and a female thread on the other, used to separate and secure components in an assembly. They are commonly used in electronic and mechanical applications to provide structural support, electrical insulation, and precise spacing between parts.","nf":8},{"id":"1284","name":"Standoffs Miscell...","path":"Hardware > Electronic Hardware > Standoffs","n":296,"img":"img/1284.png","desc":"Standoffs miscell refers to a variety of standoff components used in different applications, designed to create space between two parts or to provide mounting solutions. These standoffs come in various shapes, sizes, and materials to suit specific needs in electronics, machinery, and construction.","nf":7},{"id":"1285","name":"Swage Standoffs","path":"Hardware > Electronic Hardware > Standoffs","n":5,"img":"img/1285.png","desc":"Swage standoffs are mechanical components used to create a gap between two parts by securing them together with a swaged or deformed end, providing stability and alignment. They are commonly used in electronics and assembly applications to separate and mount components securely.","nf":0}]}],"cats":[{"id":"1129","name":"Spacers","path":"Hardware > Electronic Hardware","n":791,"img":"img/1129.png","desc":"A spacer is a mechanical component used to create a gap or maintain a specific distance between two parts in an assembly. It is commonly used to ensure proper alignment, prevent contact between components, or accommodate for thermal expansion or vibration.","nf":8}]},{"name":"Caps and Plugs","n":684,"img":"img/1041.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1041","name":"General Caps and Plugs","path":"Hardware > Caps and Plugs","n":532,"img":"img/1041.png","desc":"General caps and plugs are protective components used to cover and seal openings in pipes, fittings, or machinery, preventing dirt, debris, or moisture from entering. They are commonly used in manufacturing, plumbing, and automotive applications to safeguard threaded or unthreaded holes during storage, transport, or when parts are not in use.","nf":4},{"id":"752","name":"Grommets","path":"Hardware > Caps and Plugs","n":138,"img":"img/752.png","desc":"Grommets are circular eyelets made from rubber, metal, or plastic, used to reinforce holes in materials such as fabric, leather, or metal. They provide protection against abrasion, prevent tearing, and allow for the passage of cables, wires, or ropes while maintaining structural integrity.","nf":9},{"id":"757","name":"Threaded Plugs","path":"Hardware > Caps and Plugs","n":14,"img":"img/757.png","desc":"Threaded plugs are fasteners with internal or external threads designed to seal or close off openings, such as pipe ends or threaded holes. They are commonly used in plumbing, manufacturing, and automotive industries to prevent contamination, leakage, or damage during storage or transportation.","nf":7}]},{"name":"Springs","n":673,"img":"img/760.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"760","name":"Compression Springs","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":358,"img":"img/760.png","desc":"Compression springs are coiled springs designed to resist compressive forces and return to their original length when the pressure is released. They are commonly used in a wide range of applications, including automotive, industrial machinery, and electronics, to absorb shock, store energy, or maintain pressure.","nf":5},{"id":"761","name":"Extension Springs","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":111,"img":"img/761.png","desc":"Extension springs are mechanical springs designed to stretch and return to their original shape when a pulling force is applied. They are commonly used in applications like garage doors, trampolines, and machinery to store and release energy, providing tension or resisting external forces.","nf":5},{"id":"1251","name":"Springs Misc..","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":86,"img":"img/1251.png","desc":"Spring miscellaneous (misc.) refers to a collection of various spring types and related components that serve different functions in mechanical systems. These can include compression springs, torsion springs, extension springs, and other specialty springs used in diverse applications such as automotive, industrial machinery, and consumer products.","nf":4},{"id":"764","name":"Torsion Springs","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":34,"img":"img/764.png","desc":"Torsion springs are mechanical springs that store and release rotational energy when twisted or wound. They are commonly used in applications such as garage doors, clipboards, and automotive components to provide controlled movement and force.","nf":4},{"id":"762","name":"Gas Spring Ball Studs","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":32,"img":"img/762.png","desc":"Gas spring ball studs are fasteners designed to provide a secure pivot or attachment point for gas springs, allowing smooth movement and force distribution. They typically feature a ball-shaped end that fits into a corresponding socket or mounting bracket, enabling easy assembly and adjustment in applications like automotive and industrial equipment.","nf":11},{"id":"763","name":"Multi-Wave Compression Springs","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":23,"img":"img/763.png","desc":"Multi-wave compression springs are specialized springs that consist of multiple waves or coils stacked together, designed to provide increased strength and resistance in a compact form. They are commonly used in applications where space is limited, such as in automotive, aerospace, and industrial machinery, to absorb shock or store mechanical energy.","nf":5},{"id":"1327","name":"Only SBS","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":22,"img":"","desc":"","nf":0},{"id":"1250","name":"Leaf Springs","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":5,"img":"img/1250.png","desc":"Leaf springs are a type of suspension component made of multiple layers of metal strips (leaves) that are stacked together to form a flexible, curved shape. They are commonly used in vehicles, particularly in heavy-duty trucks and trailers, to absorb shock and support the weight of the vehicle.","nf":1},{"id":"1287","name":"Conical Compression Spring","path":"Hardware > Springs","n":2,"img":"img/1287.png","desc":"A conical compression spring is a type of mechanical spring that has a tapered shape, with a smaller diameter at one end and a larger diameter at the other. This design allows for a more compact spring that provides high force in a limited space, commonly used in applications where variable load requirements are needed.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Strut Clamps and Hangers","n":58,"img":"img/767.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"767","name":"Pipe, Tube and Conduit Hangers","path":"Hardware > Strut Clamps and Hangers","n":27,"img":"img/767.png","desc":"Pipe, tube, and conduit hangers are support brackets or fasteners used to suspend and secure pipes, tubes, or electrical conduits in place. These hangers help maintain proper alignment, prevent damage, and ensure safety in various construction, plumbing, and electrical applications.","nf":3},{"id":"770","name":"Channel Nuts","path":"Hardware > Strut Clamps and Hangers","n":13,"img":"img/770.png","desc":"Channel nuts are fasteners designed to fit into the channels of metal framing systems, providing a secure point for attaching bolts or screws. They are commonly used in construction and industrial applications to create adjustable and easily modified connections within structural frameworks.","nf":3},{"id":"1039","name":"Strut Bracket","path":"Hardware > Strut Clamps and Hangers","n":9,"img":"img/1039.png","desc":"A strut bracket is a metal or structural component used to support and stabilize struts in mechanical or construction applications. It helps secure the strut in place, ensuring proper alignment and load distribution in systems like suspension, scaffolding, or structural frameworks.","nf":1},{"id":"765","name":"Beam Clamps","path":"Hardware > Strut Clamps and Hangers","n":5,"img":"img/765.png","desc":"Beam clamps are adjustable fastening devices used to attach pipes, cables, or other equipment to structural beams or supports. They provide a secure, easy-to-install solution for suspending or supporting components in industrial and construction applications.","nf":1},{"id":"768","name":"Split Ring Hangers","path":"Hardware > Strut Clamps and Hangers","n":4,"img":"img/768.png","desc":"Split ring hangers are mechanical fasteners designed to securely suspend pipes, cables, or rods from a ceiling or structure using a circular ring that is split to allow easy installation. They provide reliable support and are commonly used in plumbing, electrical, and HVAC systems for overhead installations.","nf":0}]}],"cats":[{"id":"50","name":"Hardware Kits","path":"Hardware","n":2056,"img":"img/50.png","desc":"Hardware kits are packaged sets that contain a variety of fasteners, tools, and components designed for specific tasks or projects, such as assembly, repairs, or installations. These kits provide convenience and ensure that all necessary parts are available in one package, often used in automotive, construction, or home improvement applications.","nf":0},{"id":"36","name":"Door Lock / Component","path":"Hardware","n":160,"img":"img/36.png","desc":"A door lock is a mechanical or electronic device used to secure a door, preventing unauthorized access while allowing authorized users to open it. Door lock components include the lock cylinder, key, latch, strike plate, and bolts, all working together to provide security and functionality.","nf":5},{"id":"30","name":"Braces / Brackets","path":"Hardware","n":109,"img":"img/30.png","desc":"Braces and brackets are structural supports used to reinforce or stabilize objects by providing additional strength or fixing them to a surface. They are commonly used in construction, furniture assembly, and machinery to enhance stability and prevent movement or distortion of components.","nf":5}]},{"name":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":1594,"img":"img/1046.png","kids":[{"name":"Clamps and Collars","n":892,"img":"img/1046.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1046","name":"Hose Clamps","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Clamps and Collars","n":590,"img":"img/1046.png","desc":"Hose clamps are fastening devices used to secure hoses onto fittings or connectors, preventing leaks and ensuring a tight seal. They typically consist of a metal band with a screw mechanism that tightens around the hose, creating pressure to keep it in place.","nf":14},{"id":"1045","name":"Ear Clamps","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Clamps and Collars","n":242,"img":"img/1045.png","desc":"Ear clamps are a type of fastening device commonly used to secure hoses or tubing onto fittings, providing a tight seal to prevent leaks. They feature a unique \"ear\" that is crimped over the hose, ensuring a secure and durable connection.","nf":10},{"id":"1236","name":"Clamp Tools","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Clamps and Collars","n":22,"img":"img/1236.png","desc":"Clamp tools are devices used to securely hold objects in place while performing tasks like cutting, welding, or assembly. They provide stable support by applying pressure to the workpiece, ensuring precision and safety during operations in woodworking, metalworking, and other industries.","nf":0},{"id":"1049","name":"Uni Clamps","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Clamps and Collars","n":16,"img":"img/1049.png","desc":"Uni clamps are versatile fastening components used to secure pipes, hoses, or cables in place, typically featuring a robust design for easy installation and strong hold. They are commonly used in plumbing, automotive, and industrial applications to organize and support various components, ensuring stability and safety.","nf":2},{"id":"1280","name":"Fixing Clips and Straps","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Clamps and Collars","n":13,"img":"img/1280.png","desc":"Fixing clips and straps are fastening devices used to secure objects, such as cables, wires, or pipes, to surfaces or structures. Clips hold items in place with a snap-on mechanism, while straps use adjustable tension to tightly bind and support the items, ensuring stability and organization.","nf":0},{"id":"1048","name":"T Bolt Clamps","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Clamps and Collars","n":9,"img":"img/1048.png","desc":"T-bolt clamps are adjustable fasteners used to secure hoses or pipes, typically in high-pressure or high-torque applications. They feature a T-shaped bolt that tightens the band around the hose, providing a strong and reliable seal to prevent leaks or disconnections.","nf":1}]},{"name":"Fittings","n":246,"img":"img/1058.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1058","name":"Nipples","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Fittings","n":110,"img":"img/1058.png","desc":"Nipples are short, cylindrical pipe fittings used to connect two other pipes or components in a piping system. Typically threaded on both ends, they are commonly used in plumbing, HVAC, and industrial applications to extend or connect pipes in various directions.","nf":4},{"id":"1053","name":"Barbed Fittings","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Fittings","n":91,"img":"img/1053.png","desc":"Barbed fittings are plumbing and hose connectors with raised ridges or \"barbs\" that securely grip and hold flexible tubing in place. They are commonly used in applications involving fluid or gas transfer, ensuring a leak-free connection by preventing the hose from slipping off the fitting.","nf":8},{"id":"1062","name":"Tee Fittings","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Fittings","n":27,"img":"img/1062.png","desc":"Tee fittings are plumbing or piping connectors shaped like the letter \"T,\" designed to join three pipes or tubes at a 90-degree angle. They are commonly used in fluid or gas systems to create branches, allowing for the distribution or redirection of flow in various directions.","nf":3},{"id":"1060","name":"Compression Fittings","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics > Fittings","n":18,"img":"img/1060.png","desc":"Compression fittings are mechanical connectors used to join two pipes or tubes by compressing a fitting onto the tube with a ferrule or sleeve, creating a secure, leak-proof seal. They are commonly used in plumbing, gas, and hydraulic systems for their simplicity and ability to handle high-pressure applications.","nf":2}]}],"cats":[{"id":"157","name":"Flanges, Gaskets, and Gasket Materials","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":224,"img":"","desc":"","nf":5},{"id":"1056","name":"Elbows","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":85,"img":"img/1056.png","desc":"Elbows are pipe fittings used to change the direction of a pipe or tubing, typically at a 90-degree or 45-degree angle. They are commonly made from materials like metal, plastic, or PVC and are used in plumbing, HVAC, and other piping systems to navigate around obstacles or alter flow paths.","nf":4},{"id":"94","name":"Hose / Hose Reels","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":60,"img":"img/94.png","desc":"Hoses are flexible tubes used for transporting fluids or gases in various applications, such as watering, industrial processes, or cleaning. Hose reels are storage devices that organize and retract hoses neatly, preventing tangling and damage while allowing for easy deployment and use.","nf":6},{"id":"93","name":"Hose End Fittings","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":55,"img":"img/93.png","desc":"Hose end fittings (or elbows) are connectors designed to attach hoses to other components, such as pipes or valves, ensuring a secure and leak-free connection. They come in various shapes and sizes, typically featuring threads or barbs to fit a wide range of hose types and applications.","nf":4},{"id":"1061","name":"Compression Nuts","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":20,"img":"img/1061.png","desc":"Compression nuts are specialized fasteners designed to apply pressure and create a tight seal between two components, often used in plumbing or fluid systems. They are commonly used to secure pipes or tubes to fittings, preventing leaks and ensuring a strong, leak-proof connection.","nf":7},{"id":"1065","name":"Pneumatic Coup Plug","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":10,"img":"img/1065.png","desc":"A pneumatic coupler plug is a fitting used to connect or disconnect pneumatic hoses, tools, or equipment quickly and securely in compressed air systems. It features a male plug that mates with a corresponding female coupler, providing a leak-proof connection for air flow.","nf":0},{"id":"1064","name":"Hose Couplers/Access","path":"Hydraulics And Pneumatics","n":2,"img":"img/1064.png","desc":"Hose couplers are devices used to connect and disconnect hoses quickly and securely, enabling the transfer of fluids or gases between different systems. They come in various designs, including threaded, push-fit, or quick-connect types, offering flexibility for different applications in industrial, agricultural, and automotive settings.","nf":1}]},{"name":"Electrical","n":1334,"img":"img/1254.png","kids":[{"name":"Wire And Tube Management","n":869,"img":"img/1254.png","kids":[{"name":"Cable Ties","n":557,"img":"img/1254.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1254","name":"General Cable Ties","path":"Electrical > Wire And Tube Management > Cable Ties","n":427,"img":"img/1254.png","desc":"General cable ties are versatile fastening tools used to bundle and secure cables, wires, or other items together, ensuring organization and preventing tangling. They are typically made of durable materials like nylon and feature a ratcheting mechanism for easy tightening and a secure hold.","nf":6},{"id":"1087","name":"Mounting Cable Ties","path":"Electrical > Wire And Tube Management > Cable Ties","n":130,"img":"img/1087.png","desc":"Mounting cable ties are fasteners designed to secure and organize cables or wires by attaching them to a surface using an integrated mounting base. They provide a neat, secure, and permanent solution for managing cables in various applications, such as electrical systems, machinery, or construction.","nf":5}]}],"cats":[{"id":"1083","name":"Wiring, Tube and Loop Cable Clamps","path":"Electrical > Wire And Tube Management","n":312,"img":"img/1083.png","desc":"Wiring, tube, and loop cable clamps are devices used to secure and organize cables, tubes, or wires, preventing them from tangling or moving during operation. These clamps typically feature a loop design to hold the cables in place, ensuring safety and order in various mechanical or electrical systems.","nf":11}]},{"name":"Terminals and Wire Connectors","n":281,"img":"img/1082.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1082","name":"Terminals","path":"Electrical > Terminals and Wire Connectors","n":216,"img":"img/1082.png","desc":"Terminals are electrical connectors used to attach wires or cables to a device, allowing for the transfer of electrical signals or power. They come in various types, such as ring, spade, and bullet terminals, and are commonly used in automotive, industrial, and electrical applications for secure and reliable connections.","nf":0},{"id":"1081","name":"Ferrules","path":"Electrical > Terminals and Wire Connectors","n":65,"img":"img/1081.png","desc":"Ferrules are cylindrical fittings used to reinforce or protect the ends of wires, cables, or rods by providing a secure connection or preventing fraying. They are commonly used in electrical, plumbing, and mechanical applications to ensure durability, safety, and proper performance.","nf":5}]},{"name":"Conduit and Accessories","n":92,"img":"img/1069.png","kids":[{"name":"Conduit Fittings","n":61,"img":"img/1069.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1069","name":"Conduit Bushings","path":"Electrical > Conduit and Accessories > Conduit Fittings","n":61,"img":"img/1069.png","desc":"Conduit bushings are protective fittings used at the ends of electrical conduits to prevent damage to wires and cables by providing a smooth, secure connection. They help ensure safety by preventing wire abrasion and offering grounding continuity in electrical systems.","nf":6}]}],"cats":[{"id":"1252","name":"Expandable Sleeving","path":"Electrical > Conduit and Accessories","n":15,"img":"img/1252.png","desc":"Expandable sleeving is a flexible, protective cover made from materials like braided nylon or polyester that expands to fit around wires, cables, or hoses. It is commonly used in electrical and automotive applications to provide insulation, abrasion resistance, and organizational benefits while allowing for easy installation and adjustment around varying cable sizes.","nf":8},{"id":"1253","name":"Conduit and Accessories Misc.","path":"Electrical > Conduit and Accessories","n":13,"img":"img/1253.png","desc":"Conduit and accessories miscellaneous (misc.) components include a variety of parts used in electrical systems to protect and route wiring, such as junction boxes, elbows, connectors, and straps. These items help ensure the safety, organization, and stability of electrical wiring installations in both residential and industrial settings.","nf":7},{"id":"1067","name":"Electrical Compression Fittings","path":"Electrical > Conduit and Accessories","n":3,"img":"img/1067.png","desc":"Electrical compression fittings are connectors used to secure electrical cables to terminals or equipment by compressing the cable's conductors inside the fitting. They provide a reliable, durable connection that ensures proper electrical conductivity and resistance to corrosion in various industrial and commercial applications.","nf":0}]}],"cats":[{"id":"96","name":"Power Cords","path":"Electrical","n":84,"img":"img/96.png","desc":"Power cords are flexible electrical cables designed to connect electronic devices or appliances to a power source, allowing for the transmission of electrical current. They typically consist of insulated wires enclosed in a durable outer sheath, with a plug on one end and a connector on the other to ensure safe and efficient power delivery.","nf":0},{"id":"98","name":"Transformers","path":"Electrical","n":8,"img":"img/98.png","desc":"Transformers are electrical devices used to change the voltage of alternating current (AC) in a circuit, either stepping it up or stepping it down. They consist of two coils of wire wound around a magnetic core, allowing the transfer of electrical energy between the coils through electromagnetic induction.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Safety","n":797,"img":"img/1191.png","kids":[{"name":"Facility Identification","n":648,"img":"","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1321","name":"Label","path":"Safety > Facility Identification","n":576,"img":"","desc":"","nf":0},{"id":"85","name":"Special","path":"Safety > Facility Identification","n":72,"img":"","desc":"","nf":0}]},{"name":"Traffic Control","n":82,"img":"img/1191.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1191","name":"Anti Skid Tape","path":"Safety > Traffic Control","n":82,"img":"img/1191.png","desc":"Anti-skid tape is a high-friction adhesive material applied to surfaces to prevent slipping and improve traction. It is commonly used on stairs, ramps, walkways, and machinery to enhance safety in environments where slipping hazards are present.","nf":0}]}],"cats":[{"id":"153","name":"Hand Protection","path":"Safety","n":67,"img":"img/153.png","desc":"Hand protection refers to equipment or gear, such as gloves, designed to safeguard hands from potential hazards, including cuts, burns, chemicals, or impacts. It is commonly used in various industries, including construction, manufacturing, and healthcare, to ensure worker safety and prevent injuries.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Tools and Equipment","n":767,"img":"img/1259.png","kids":[{"name":"Fastener Installation and Repair Tools","n":767,"img":"img/1259.png","kids":[{"name":"Hand Tools","n":446,"img":"img/1214.png","kids":[{"name":"Key Product","n":312,"img":"","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1206","name":"Hex and Torx Key Products","path":"Tools and Equipment > Fastener Installation and Repair Tools > Hand Tools > Key Product","n":312,"img":"","desc":"","nf":2}]},{"name":"Wrench Sets and Accessories","n":114,"img":"","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1219","name":"Wrenches and Accesories","path":"Tools and Equipment > Fastener Installation and Repair Tools > Hand Tools > Wrench Sets and Accessories","n":114,"img":"","desc":"","nf":0}]},{"name":"Pliers, Pliers Sets and Accessories","n":11,"img":"img/1214.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1214","name":"Retaining and Lock Ring Pliers","path":"Tools and Equipment > Fastener Installation and Repair Tools > Hand Tools > Pliers, Pliers Sets and Accessories","n":11,"img":"img/1214.png","desc":"Retaining and lock ring pliers are specialized tools used to install or remove retaining rings and lock rings, which secure components in place within shafts, grooves, or housings. These pliers typically feature adjustable jaws and tips designed to grip and manipulate the rings without damaging them during installation or removal.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Staplers and Staples","n":9,"img":"img/1216.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1216","name":"Staples","path":"Tools and Equipment > Fastener Installation and Repair Tools > Hand Tools > Staplers and Staples","n":9,"img":"img/1216.png","desc":"Staples are small, U-shaped metal fasteners used to bind materials together, typically paper, by piercing through the sheets and folding over the edges to hold them in place. They are commonly applied using a stapler in offices, schools, and various other environments for organizing or securing documents.","nf":1}]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Power Tool Accessories","n":321,"img":"img/1259.png","kids":[{"name":"Bit Tips and Drivers","n":321,"img":"img/1259.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1259","name":"Drive Bits","path":"Tools and Equipment > Fastener Installation and Repair Tools > Power Tool Accessories > Bit Tips and Drivers","n":186,"img":"img/1259.png","desc":"Drive bits are tools used to insert or remove screws and fasteners by fitting into the corresponding drive of the screw. They come in various types, such as Phillips, flathead, or Torx, and are commonly used with power drills or screwdrivers for efficient fastening tasks.","nf":1},{"id":"1227","name":"Drivers","path":"Tools and Equipment > Fastener Installation and Repair Tools > Power Tool Accessories > Bit Tips and Drivers","n":115,"img":"img/1227.png","desc":"Drivers are tools used to insert or remove fasteners, such as screws, bolts, or pins, by applying torque to their heads. They come in various types, such as screwdrivers, impact drivers, and power drivers, each designed for specific fastener types and applications.","nf":4},{"id":"1226","name":"Bit Tip Holders","path":"Tools and Equipment > Fastener Installation and Repair Tools > Power Tool Accessories > Bit Tips and Drivers","n":20,"img":"img/1226.png","desc":"Bit tip holders are devices designed to securely hold and insert interchangeable bits into tools like drills, screwdrivers, or impact drivers. They provide a stable connection, allowing for easy swapping of bits and efficient handling during fastening or drilling tasks.","nf":2}]}],"cats":[]}],"cats":[]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking","n":755,"img":"img/1114.png","kids":[{"name":"Tooling Components","n":298,"img":"img/1123.png","kids":[{"name":"Workholding Clamp Accesories","n":118,"img":"img/1122.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1122","name":"Knobs","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Tooling Components > Workholding Clamp Accesories","n":67,"img":"img/1122.png","desc":"Knobs are small, rounded or cylindrical handles used to operate or adjust machinery, furniture, or appliances. They are commonly designed for easy gripping and turning, providing control over doors, drawers, or electronic devices in both residential and industrial settings.","nf":7},{"id":"1121","name":"Flanged Washer","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Tooling Components > Workholding Clamp Accesories","n":51,"img":"img/1121.png","desc":"A flanged washer is a type of washer with a protruding flange around its edge, designed to distribute pressure more evenly and prevent damage to the surface beneath a fastener. It is commonly used to create a larger bearing surface, enhance stability, and prevent loosening or wear in mechanical and structural applications.","nf":3}]},{"name":"Workholding Fasteners","n":68,"img":"img/1127.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1127","name":"T-Slot Bolts","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Tooling Components > Workholding Fasteners","n":29,"img":"img/1127.png","desc":"T-slot bolts are fasteners with a head shaped like the letter \"T,\" designed to fit into T-shaped slots in framing systems, allowing for easy attachment and adjustment. They are commonly used in industrial applications, such as assembling modular structures, conveyors, or machinery, where precise alignment and secure fastening are essential.","nf":8},{"id":"1128","name":"T-Slot Nuts","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Tooling Components > Workholding Fasteners","n":24,"img":"img/1128.png","desc":"T-slot nuts are fasteners designed to fit into the T-shaped slots of a metal framing system, providing a secure anchor point for other components or machinery. They are commonly used in modular assembly systems, such as workbenches or machine tools, to easily adjust and reconfigure setups.","nf":6},{"id":"1125","name":"Screw Clamps Assemblies","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Tooling Components > Workholding Fasteners","n":15,"img":"img/1125.png","desc":"Screw clamp assemblies are fastening systems that use a threaded screw mechanism to tightly secure and hold components in place, often providing adjustable clamping force. These assemblies are commonly used in mechanical, electrical, and construction applications where strong, reliable pressure is needed to hold parts together.","nf":5}]}],"cats":[{"id":"1123","name":"Plungers and Accessories","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Tooling Components","n":112,"img":"img/1123.png","desc":"Plungers and accessories are mechanical components used for precise positioning, locking, or adjusting in various machinery and equipment. Plungers typically feature a spring-loaded pin that can be extended or retracted, while accessories like handles or brackets facilitate easy operation and customization for different applications.","nf":7}]},{"name":"Holemaking / Drill","n":281,"img":"img/1114.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1114","name":"Screw Machine Drills","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Holemaking / Drill","n":281,"img":"img/1114.png","desc":"Screw machine drills are high-precision drilling tools commonly used in manufacturing to create small, accurate holes in a variety of materials. They are designed for use in screw machines or automatic drilling equipment, offering fast, consistent performance in high-volume production settings.","nf":3}]},{"name":"Threading and Tapping","n":145,"img":"img/1116.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1116","name":"Taps","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Threading and Tapping","n":145,"img":"img/1116.png","desc":"Taps are cutting tools used to create internal threads in a hole, enabling the insertion of screws or bolts. They are commonly used in machining and metalworking to enable secure and precise threaded connections in a variety of materials.","nf":5}]},{"name":"Machine Tool","n":31,"img":"img/1115.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1115","name":"Hand Knobs and Wheel","path":"Cutting Tools and Metalworking > Machine Tool","n":31,"img":"img/1115.png","desc":"Hand knobs and wheels are manual fastening tools designed for easy adjustment or operation by hand. They provide a convenient grip for tightening or loosening components, often used in machinery, equipment, or furniture for quick and secure adjustments without the need for additional tools.","nf":7}]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Raw Materials","n":717,"img":"img/1188.png","kids":[{"name":"Keyed Shafts and Keys","n":550,"img":"","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"147","name":"Keys and Keystock","path":"Raw Materials > Keyed Shafts and Keys","n":550,"img":"","desc":"","nf":4}]},{"name":"Sheet Stock Material","n":127,"img":"img/1188.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1188","name":"Sheet Material","path":"Raw Materials > Sheet Stock Material","n":127,"img":"img/1188.png","desc":"Sheet material refers to flat, thin, and flexible materials, often manufactured in large, uniform sizes, used in various applications such as construction, manufacturing, or design. Common types of sheet materials include metal, plastic, wood, and rubber, each offering specific properties suited to different purposes.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Bar Stock","n":21,"img":"img/1181.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1181","name":"Round Bar Stock","path":"Raw Materials > Bar Stock","n":21,"img":"img/1181.png","desc":"Round bar stock is a cylindrical piece of metal, typically made of steel, aluminum, or other alloys, used as a raw material in manufacturing. It is commonly used in machining, fabrication, and construction to create custom parts, shafts, or fasteners.","nf":3}]}],"cats":[{"id":"145","name":"Extrusion","path":"Raw Materials","n":10,"img":"img/145.png","desc":"Extrusion is a manufacturing process in which material, often metal, plastic, or rubber, is forced through a die to create long shapes with a fixed cross-sectional profile. This process is commonly used in industries to produce products like pipes, profiles, and sheets in continuous lengths.","nf":0},{"id":"146","name":"Glass Beads","path":"Raw Materials","n":9,"img":"img/146.png","desc":"Glass beads are small, spherical particles made from glass, commonly used for applications such as surface finishing, reflective coatings, or as a blasting medium in industrial processes. They are known for their durability, smooth surface, and ability to provide uniform abrasion or enhance visibility through reflective properties.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Plumbing","n":455,"img":"img/1162.png","kids":[{"name":"Pipe Fittings","n":299,"img":"img/1162.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1162","name":"Pipe Plugs","path":"Plumbing > Pipe Fittings","n":232,"img":"img/1162.png","desc":"Pipe plugs are devices used to seal the ends of pipes to prevent the passage of fluids, gases, or contaminants. They are commonly used in plumbing, construction, and industrial applications to temporarily or permanently block pipe openings.","nf":13},{"id":"1161","name":"Pipe Couplings","path":"Plumbing > Pipe Fittings","n":37,"img":"img/1161.png","desc":"Pipe couplings are fittings used to join two sections of pipe together, allowing for the extension or repair of a piping system. They come in various designs, including threaded, slip-on, and compression types, and are used in plumbing, industrial, and fluid transport systems.","nf":7},{"id":"1159","name":"Pipe Bushing","path":"Plumbing > Pipe Fittings","n":27,"img":"img/1159.png","desc":"A pipe bushing is a fitting used to reduce the size of a pipe opening, allowing a smaller pipe to be connected to a larger one. It is commonly used in plumbing, electrical, and industrial applications to create a secure, leak-proof connection between pipes of different diameters.","nf":11},{"id":"1163","name":"Pipe Reducers","path":"Plumbing > Pipe Fittings","n":3,"img":"img/1163.png","desc":"Pipe reducers are fittings used to connect two pipes of different diameters, allowing for a smooth transition from a larger to a smaller pipe or vice versa. They are commonly employed in plumbing, HVAC, and industrial systems to control flow rates and adapt to varying pipe sizes.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Tubing and Tubing Accessories","n":141,"img":"img/1167.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1167","name":"Tubing","path":"Plumbing > Tubing and Tubing Accessories","n":141,"img":"img/1167.png","desc":"Tubing is a flexible or rigid hollow material, typically made from metal, plastic, or rubber, used to transport fluids, gases, or other substances in various systems. It is commonly used in plumbing, HVAC, medical devices, and industrial applications due to its ability to be shaped and cut to specific lengths for efficient fluid or gas transfer.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Plumbing Valves and Accessories","n":15,"img":"","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"133","name":"Plumbing Valves and Accessories","path":"Plumbing > Plumbing Valves and Accessories","n":15,"img":"","desc":"","nf":3}]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Packaging and Shipping Products","n":449,"img":"img/1158.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1158","name":"Boxes and Cartons","path":"Packaging and Shipping Products","n":184,"img":"img/1158.png","desc":"Boxes and cartons are containers used for storing, protecting, and transporting goods. Boxes are typically smaller, often with flaps that can be folded or sealed, while cartons are larger, more rigid boxes used for bulk storage and shipping.","nf":0},{"id":"1149","name":"Bins","path":"Packaging and Shipping Products","n":150,"img":"img/1149.png","desc":"Bins are storage containers used to hold, organize, and transport items in a variety of settings, such as warehouses, kitchens, or offices. They come in various sizes and materials, such as plastic or metal, to accommodate different types of goods and enhance efficiency in storage and retrieval.","nf":0},{"id":"1146","name":"Bag","path":"Packaging and Shipping Products","n":115,"img":"img/1146.png","desc":"A bag is a flexible container typically made of fabric, plastic, or paper, designed to carry, store, or transport items. It can vary in size, shape, and style, and is commonly used in retail, travel, and personal storage applications.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Power Transmission","n":436,"img":"img/1175.png","kids":[{"name":"Collars, Couplings, and Components","n":196,"img":"img/1175.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1175","name":"Shaft Collars","path":"Power Transmission > Collars, Couplings, and Components","n":196,"img":"img/1175.png","desc":"Shaft collars are cylindrical components that are mounted on a shaft to secure, position, or limit the movement of other parts in mechanical assemblies. They are commonly used in applications such as bearings, gears, or sprockets, to prevent axial displacement.","nf":6}]},{"name":"Bearings","n":150,"img":"img/1258.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"135","name":"Bearing and Components","path":"Power Transmission > Bearings","n":99,"img":"","desc":"","nf":5},{"id":"1258","name":"Flanged Bushing","path":"Power Transmission > Bearings","n":36,"img":"img/1258.png","desc":"A flanged bushing is a cylindrical bearing with a flange on one end, designed to provide support and reduce friction between two moving parts. It is commonly used in machinery or automotive applications to guide shafts or pins while ensuring proper alignment and load distribution.","nf":8},{"id":"1171","name":"Sleeve Bearings","path":"Power Transmission > Bearings","n":15,"img":"img/1171.png","desc":"Sleeve bearings are simple, cylindrical bearings that support a rotating shaft or component, reducing friction and wear between moving parts. They are often made of materials like bronze, steel, or plastic and are commonly used in applications where low cost and low maintenance are important, such as in motors, pumps, and conveyors.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Unmounted Bearing","n":22,"img":"img/1180.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1180","name":"Rod Ends","path":"Power Transmission > Unmounted Bearing","n":22,"img":"img/1180.png","desc":"Rod ends are mechanical components used to connect rods or shafts to other parts, typically featuring a spherical bearing that allows for angular movement. They are commonly used in linkages, steering systems, and control mechanisms, providing flexibility and stability in mechanical assemblies.","nf":9}]},{"name":"Seals and Accessories","n":10,"img":"img/1177.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1177","name":"Oil Seals","path":"Power Transmission > Seals and Accessories","n":10,"img":"img/1177.png","desc":"Oil seals are mechanical components designed to prevent the leakage of lubricants or oils while keeping contaminants out of machinery or equipment. Typically made of rubber or elastomers, they are used in rotating or moving parts such as engines, pumps, and gearboxes to maintain proper lubrication and prevent wear.","nf":5}]}],"cats":[{"id":"1173","name":"Thrust Washers","path":"Power Transmission","n":58,"img":"img/1173.png","desc":"Thrust washers are flat, disk-shaped components used to provide a bearing surface for axial loads, preventing direct contact between moving parts. They are commonly used in machinery, automotive, and industrial applications to reduce friction and wear while maintaining alignment of rotating components.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Sealing","n":407,"img":"img/158.png","kids":[{"name":"Rotary and Linear Seals","n":90,"img":"img/1196.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1196","name":"Sealing Rings","path":"Sealing > Rotary and Linear Seals","n":79,"img":"img/1196.png","desc":"Sealing rings are circular components used to create a tight seal between two mating surfaces, preventing leakage of fluids or gases. They are commonly made of rubber, metal, or other materials and are used in various applications such as plumbing, automotive, and industrial machinery.","nf":6},{"id":"1268","name":"Trims","path":"Sealing > Rotary and Linear Seals","n":11,"img":"img/1268.png","desc":"Trims are decorative or protective elements applied to the edges, corners, or surfaces of objects, such as furniture, vehicles, or buildings, to enhance their appearance or provide functional protection. They can be made from various materials like wood, metal, or plastic and are commonly used in interior design, construction, and automotive industries.","nf":2}]}],"cats":[{"id":"158","name":"O-rings","path":"Sealing","n":317,"img":"img/158.png","desc":"O-rings are circular seals made from elastomeric materials, designed to fit into grooves and prevent the leakage of liquids or gases between two surfaces. They are widely used in various industries, including automotive, aerospace, and plumbing, for their reliability in creating airtight or watertight seals.","nf":4}]},{"name":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":191,"img":"img/1142.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1142","name":"S Hooks","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":63,"img":"img/1142.png","desc":"S hooks are metal hooks shaped like the letter \"S\" that are used to hang, link, or attach items in a variety of applications. They are commonly used in storage, organizing, and industrial settings due to their ease of use and ability to quickly secure items without the need for tools.","nf":6},{"id":"121","name":"Lifting Eye Bolts","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":38,"img":"img/121.png","desc":"Lifting eye bolts are threaded bolts with a looped or circular eye at the top, designed to provide a secure point for attaching lifting equipment to a load. They are commonly used in industrial, construction, and shipping applications to safely lift and move heavy or bulky items.","nf":6},{"id":"122","name":"Lifting Eye Nuts","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":24,"img":"img/122.png","desc":"A lifting eye nut is a metal fastener with a threaded interior and a looped exterior designed for attaching lifting equipment, allowing for safe and secure lifting of heavy loads. It is typically used in construction, manufacturing, and heavy equipment industries for rigging and lifting purposes.","nf":6},{"id":"1140","name":"Hoist Rings","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":23,"img":"img/1140.png","desc":"Hoist rings are heavy-duty lifting devices designed to provide a secure attachment point for lifting and hoisting heavy loads. They typically feature a rotating ring to allow for multi-directional movement and are commonly used in industrial and construction applications.","nf":6},{"id":"1154","name":"Wire Rope Clips","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":21,"img":"img/1154.png","desc":"Wire rope clips are mechanical devices used to secure the ends of a wire rope by clamping the rope to itself, forming a loop or connection. They are commonly used in rigging, construction, and industrial applications to ensure a strong, secure attachment and prevent the rope from unraveling.","nf":3},{"id":"1256","name":"Fork Head","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":13,"img":"img/1256.png","desc":"A fork head is a type of fastener or tool attachment that features a fork-like shape, typically used to engage with or secure a component. Commonly found in mechanical and automotive applications, it is designed to provide leverage or hold parts in place during assembly or maintenance.","nf":2},{"id":"120","name":"Drop-N-Tell","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":7,"img":"img/120.png","desc":"Drop-N-Tell is a type of impact indicator used to visually indicate whether a package or shipment has been subjected to excessive force or dropped during transit. The device contains a red indicator that is triggered when the package experiences a certain level of impact, providing a clear sign of potential damage to the contents.","nf":0},{"id":"1136","name":"Bolt Snaps","path":"Material Handling, Lifting and Rigging","n":2,"img":"img/1136.png","desc":"Bolt snaps are metal fasteners with a spring-loaded mechanism and a hook-shaped design, used to quickly and securely attach or detach items. They are commonly used in applications such as pet leashes, keychains, and securing equipment in outdoor or industrial settings.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Test and Measurement","n":116,"img":"img/902.png","kids":[{"name":"Precision Measuring Tools","n":116,"img":"img/902.png","kids":[{"name":"Gauges","n":102,"img":"img/902.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"902","name":"Ring Gauges","path":"Test and Measurement > Precision Measuring Tools > Gauges","n":102,"img":"img/902.png","desc":"Ring gauges are precision tools used to measure the outside diameter of cylindrical objects, ensuring they meet specified tolerances. They are typically used in manufacturing and quality control to verify the accuracy and consistency of parts such as shafts, bolts, or pins.","nf":1}]}],"cats":[{"id":"903","name":"Rules","path":"Test and Measurement > Precision Measuring Tools","n":14,"img":"img/903.png","desc":"A ruler is a measuring tool typically used to determine the length or distance of objects, commonly marked in units such as inches or centimeters. It is a flat, straight instrument made of materials like plastic, metal, or wood, often used in drafting, construction, or daily tasks requiring precise measurements.","nf":0}]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Fleet and Automotive","n":114,"img":"img/103.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"103","name":"Shock Bushing","path":"Fleet and Automotive","n":114,"img":"img/103.png","desc":"A shock bushing is a rubber or elastomeric component designed to absorb and dampen vibrations, shocks, or impacts in mechanical systems. It is commonly used in automotive, industrial, and machinery applications to reduce wear and improve the longevity of parts by minimizing the transmission of forces.","nf":9}]},{"name":"Lubricants, Coolants And Fluids","n":52,"img":"img/1134.png","kids":[{"name":"Grease Fittings and Accessories","n":52,"img":"img/1134.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1134","name":"Grease Fittings","path":"Lubricants, Coolants And Fluids > Grease Fittings and Accessories","n":52,"img":"img/1134.png","desc":"Grease fittings, also known as Zerk fittings, are small metal components installed in machinery or vehicles to provide a point for injecting grease or lubricants into moving parts. They are commonly used in automotive, industrial, and agricultural applications to reduce friction, prevent wear, and extend the life of mechanical systems.","nf":12}]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Abrasives","n":34,"img":"img/1106.png","kids":[{"name":"Brushes and Deburring Products","n":26,"img":"img/1106.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1106","name":"Wire Brush","path":"Abrasives > Brushes and Deburring Products","n":22,"img":"img/1106.png","desc":"A wire brush is a cleaning tool consisting of metal bristles attached to a handle or wheel, used to remove rust, dirt, paint, or debris from surfaces. It is commonly employed in construction, maintenance, and metalworking tasks to prepare surfaces for further treatment or finishing.","nf":3},{"id":"1105","name":"Deburring Tools","path":"Abrasives > Brushes and Deburring Products","n":4,"img":"img/1105.png","desc":"Deburring tools are hand tools or machines used to remove rough edges, burrs, or sharp edges from metal, plastic, or other materials after cutting, machining, or casting. They help improve the surface finish, prevent injuries, and ensure the proper fit of components in mechanical assemblies.","nf":0}]},{"name":"Carbide Burrs Products","n":8,"img":"","kids":[{"name":"Carbide Burrs","n":8,"img":"","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"106","name":"Carbide Burrs Products","path":"Abrasives > Carbide Burrs Products > Carbide Burrs","n":8,"img":"","desc":"","nf":2}]}],"cats":[]}],"cats":[]},{"name":"Other","n":33,"img":"img/175.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"175","name":"Nuts Misc","path":"Other","n":18,"img":"img/175.png","desc":"\"Nuts Misc\" refers to a broad category of nuts used in various applications, encompassing a range of shapes, sizes, and materials for securing bolts, screws, or other fasteners. These nuts can include special types like wing nuts, lock nuts, and flange nuts, each designed for specific needs in mechanical, electrical, or construction settings.","nf":7},{"id":"898","name":"Indicators and Calipers","path":"Other","n":15,"img":"","desc":"","nf":0}]},{"name":"Adhesives, Sealants and Tape","n":24,"img":"img/1109.png","kids":[{"name":"Threadlocking Chemicals","n":24,"img":"img/1109.png","kids":[],"cats":[{"id":"1109","name":"Threadlockers","path":"Adhesives, Sealants and Tape > Threadlocking Chemicals","n":24,"img":"img/1109.png","desc":"Threadlockers are adhesive compounds applied to threaded fasteners to prevent them from loosening due to vibration, thermal expansion, or other external forces. They are commonly used in mechanical, automotive, and industrial applications to enhance the security and reliability of bolted joints.","nf":0}]}],"cats":[]}],"cats":[]},"https://s3.amazonaws.com/sbs.pod/");